\par\par \b \uc2 WEEKAHEAD-AFRICA- \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 - Kenya's shilling to weaken, Ghana cedi to firm\b0\par\par\uc2 755 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Dezember 2022\par 13:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 NAIROBI, Dec 8 (Reuters) - Kenya's shilling and Zambia's kwacha are expected to weaken against the dollar in the next week to Thursday while the Nigerian naira, Tanzania's and Uganda's shillings as well as Ghana cedi will strengthen, traders said.\par \par \uc2 KENYA\par \par \uc2 Kenya's shilling is forecast to weaken as importers seek dollars to complete orders ahead of the holiday period when market activity cools.\par \par \uc2 Commercial banks quoted the shilling at 122.70/90 per dollar, compared to 122.45/65 at last Thursday's close.\par \par \uc2 In the medium term the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to offer more support to the market when the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 's board approve the release of $433 million of funding which was approved in principle in November.\par \par \uc2 The shilling has lost 7.9% of its value against the greenback since the start of the year, touching fresh lows of 122.80/123.00 on Thursday morning, according to Refinitiv data.\par \par \uc2 "We haven't seen \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a few weeks," said a trader at one commercial bank.\par \par \uc2 "We expect demand to slow down a bit towards the end of the year. Importers are covering themselves for the Christmas period."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says it only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out any volatility in the shilling's trade and it has no preferred rate for it.\par \par \uc2 UGANDA\par \par \uc2 Uganda shilling is expected to firm, underpinned by increased dollar inflows from remittances and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest lending rate decision.\par \par \uc2 Commercial banks quoted the shilling at 3,685/3,695, compared to last Thursday's close of 3,735/3,745.\par \par \uc2 The market was receiving plentiful inflows from Ugandans working outside the country who had returned for December holidays, said one independent \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader in the capital Kampala.\par \par \uc2 "We have a lot of flows from that source (Diaspora workers)," he said, and added the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to leave its tight policy stance unchanged this week even after inflation eased would help add extra support to the local unit.\par \par \uc2 Bank of Uganda\uc2  on Wednesday left its benchmark rate unchanged at 10% despite a slight decline in inflation in November.\par \par \uc2 GHANA\par \par \uc2 Ghana's cedi is expected to appreciate this week on the back of decreased demand for dollars as companies begin to close for year-end holidays.\par \par \uc2 Refinitiv Eikon data showed the cedi trading at 12.5 to the dollar on Thursday, from 13.8 at last Thursday's close.\par \par \uc2 "We expect the narrative to continue into next week as some corporates prepare to close shop for the Christmas festivities," said Christopher Nettey, head of trading at \uc2 Stanbic Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But he noted speculative activity around a debt exchange programme announced last week could offset the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's newly-found stability.\par \par \uc2 TANZANIA\par \par \uc2 Tanzania\u8217\'20\'19s shilling is expected to gain slightly as dollar inflows into sectors such as construction boost the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Commercial banks quoted the shilling at 2,328/2,338 on Thursday, the same level as last Thursday's close.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGiven stronger economic growth recorded in the second quarter, we expect the Shilling to appreciate marginally against the dollar by the end of the year,\u8221\'20\'1D a dealer in one of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading firms, said.\par \par \uc2 ZAMBIA\par \par \uc2 The kwacha is likely to continue gradually depreciating against the dollar as demand for hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  outweighs supply.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, commercial banks quoted the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Africa's second-largest copper producer at 17.4700 per dollar from 17.2700 at the close of business a week ago.\par \par \uc2 "The kwacha is anticipated to experience losses in the near-term," \uc2 Access Bank\uc2  said in a note on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 NIGERIA\par \par \uc2 Nigeria's naira is expected to recover on the parallel market after easing within the week as diaspora remittances lift the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of the Christmas session and as businesses close for the year, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The naira was quoted at 750 to the dollar on the parallel market on Thursday, compared to 745 at last Thursday's close. It traded within a range of 445 to 447 on the official market.\par \par \uc2 "We expect the naira to recover somewhat in the coming week or so, helped by diaspora remittances and businesses winding down for the Christmas holidays," \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading firm AZA Finance said in a note. (Reporting by Hereward Holland, Chris Mfula, Elias Biryabarema, Christian Akorlie, Nuzulack Dausen and Chijioke Ohuocha; Compiled by George Obulutsa; Editing by James Macharia Chege) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-12-8T13:06:37.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221208eic80131l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
