\par\par \b \uc2 African Markets - Factors to watch on Sept 21\b0\par\par\uc2 383 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 2020\par 07:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     NAIROBI, Sept 21 - The following company announcements, scheduled economic indicators, debt\par and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market moves and political events may affect African markets on Monday.\par     - - - - -\par  GLOBAL MARKETS\par      Asian shares and most \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  held tight ranges on\par  Monday, as investors awaited developments on U.S. fiscal\par  stimulus and coronavirus vaccines amid a resurgence of\par  infections in Europe.                       \par  \par  WORLD OIL PRICES\par       Oil prices edged higher on Monday as a tropical storm\par  took aim for the U.S. Gulf of Mexico region halting some\par  production, though price gains were capped by the potential\par  return of oil output in Libya and a continued rise in\par  coronavirus cases.                 \par  \par  EMERGING MARKETS\par  For the top emerging markets news, double click on\par             \par  \par  AFRICA STOCKS\par  For the latest news on African stocks, click on     \par  \par  \par  SOUTH AFRICA MARKETS\par      South Africa's rand was steady in early trading on\par  Friday, after racing to its best in six months overnight\par  after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kept lending rates unchanged and as\par  the dollar fell following downbeat U.S. data.            \par  \par      South Africa's stock market corrected sharply during the\par  week after a strong open on Monday as poor retail sales data\par  and a host of bleak company outlooks added to the effects of\par  weaker commodity prices and quarter-end profit\par  taking.            \par  \par  SOUTH AFRICA AIRLINES\par      South Africa has pledged 10.5 billion rand ($650\par  million) to \f28 \uc2 \f2 South African Airways (SAA)\f28 \uc2 \f2 , one of the\par  administrators of the ailing state-owned airline said on\par  Friday.            \par  \par  \par  NIGERIA REVENUES\par      Nigeria's gross revenues inched up 0.8% in August to\par  682.1 billion naira ($1.79 billion) from the previous month\par  as a rise in VAT and corporate tax receipts helped offset a\par  drop in oil income, the government said.               \par  \par  KENYA MARKETS\par      The Kenyan shilling        was under pressure on Friday\par  due to demand from importers amid scarce dollar inflows, but\par  traders expected a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to buoy the\par  shilling, they said.           \par  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 KENYA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  BANKS\par      \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Kenya\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has licensed the country's first\par  mortgage refinance firm, it said on Friday, paving the way\par  for banks to access long-term finance for home\par  loans.            \par  \par  \par  \par  \par  \par  \par      For the latest precious metals report click on        \par      For the latest base metals report click on         \par      For the latest crude oil report click on\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-9-21T06:43:09.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200921eg9l00m59\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
