\par\par \b \uc2 African Markets - Factors to watch on Aug 14\b0\par\par\uc2 465 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 2020\par 07:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     NAIROBI, Aug 14 - The following company announcements, scheduled economic indicators, debt\par and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market moves and political events may affect African markets on Friday.\par     - - - - -\par  \par  \par  \par  GLOBAL MARKETS\par      Asian shares fell on Friday after lacklustre Chinese\par  economic data and worries about a delay in U.S. fiscal\par  stimulus discouraged some investors from taking on\par  risk.                       \par  \par  WORLD OIL PRICES\par      Oil prices advanced on Friday and were heading for a\par  second week of gains amid growing confidence that demand for\par  fuel is starting to pick up despite the coronavirus pandemic\par  that has slammed economies worldwide.                 \par  \par  EMERGING MARKETS\par  For the top emerging markets news, double click on\par             \par  \par  AFRICA STOCKS\par  For the latest news on African stocks, click on     \par  \par  \par  \par  SOUTH AFRICA MARKETS\par      The rand firmed against the dollar on Thursday as hopes\par  of more economic stimulus in the United States waned,\par  although fresh power cuts in South Africa limited its\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's gains.            \par  \par  SOUTH AFRICA MINING\par      South Africa's total mining output fell 28.2%\par  year-on-year in June compared to a revised contraction of\par  27.6% in May, Statistics South Africa said on\par  Thursday.            \par  \par  NIGERIA VISA BAN\par      Overturning a U.S. ban on Nigerians seeking immigrant\par  visas will take "enormous resources", but the nation is\par  making progress, President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Muhammadu Buhari\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on\par  Thursday.               \par  \par  KENYA MARKETS\par      The Kenyan shilling KES= edged higher on Thursday\par  supported by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through sale of\par  dollar to the market, traders said.            \par  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 KENYA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  BANKS\par      \f28 \uc2 \f2 KCB Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Kenya's biggest bank by assets, expects the\par  proportion of loans it will restructure due to effects of\par  the novel coronavirus to hit 25% of its total loans by\par  December, its chief executive officer said on\par  Thursday.            \par  \par  \par  MAURITIUS OIL SPILL\par      Some corals have lived for centuries at the fringes of\par  Mauritius. Now smothered for days in heavy fuel oil spilled\par  from a wrecked Japanese tanker nearby, parts of those reefs\par  may be in trouble.            \par  \par  AFRICA COVID-19\par      Seven African countries will start administering\par  coronavirus antibody tests from next week, a regional body\par  said on Thursday, as part of efforts to understand the\par  extent of the outbreak on the continent.            \par  \par  IVORY COAST PROTESTS\par      At least three people died during protests in Ivory\par  Coast on Thursday, police said, as small groups burned\par  makeshift road blocks in protests against President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alassane\par  Ouattara\f28 \uc2 \f2 's decision to stand for a third term.            \par  \par  GLOBAL OIL DEMAND\par      The \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Energy Agency\f28 \uc2 \f2  (IEA) cut its 2020 oil\par  demand forecast on Thursday, warning that reduced air travel\par  due to the coronavirus pandemic would lower global oil\par  demand this year by 8.1 million barrels per day\par  (bpd).            \par  \par  \par  \par  \par  \par  \par  \par  \par  \par      For the latest precious metals report click on        \par      For the