\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-\uc2 Kenyan  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  steps in after shilling slides\b0\par\par\uc2 514 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Juli 2019\par 14:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Updates with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 )\par     NAIROBI, July 31 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Kenya\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pumped\par dollars into the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market on Wednesday and sought\par to soak up excess liquidity after the shilling sank to\par its lowest level against the dollar in nearly five years,\par traders said.\par     The shilling has been one of Africa's top performers this\par year. But it has lost 1.2% against the dollar in the past six\par sessions due to heightened political risk at home, a stronger\par dollar, concerns about export earnings and excess liquidity in\par the money markets.\par     It fell to an intra-day low of 104.45/55 per dollar on\par Wednesday, from 103.20/30 on Monday last week, forcing the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and send it back to the 104.00 level.\par     "They sold dollars and they have beat it down to the current\par level of 104.05/25," said a senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader at a\par commercial bank.\par     The bank also sought to mop up 10 billion shillings from the\par money markets using 7 day repos, saying there was excess\par liquidity.\par     "It (shilling's drop) is also a function of liquidity.\par Yesterday (Monday) they were in the market for 35 billion," said\par a second \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader at another commercial bank.\par     The weighted average interest rate on the overnight\par borrowing market for banks has hovered around 2 percent this\par month, making it cheaper for banks to bet against the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par by buying up dollars.\par     Kenya's political risk went up a notch last week when\par Finance Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Henry Rotich\f28 \uc2 \f2  was charged in court over the loss\par of funds in tender awards for the construction of two dams. He\par denied all the charges and was freed on bail.\par     Political analysts said the charges exposed a widening\par schism between President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Uhuru Kenyatta\f28 \uc2 \f2  and his deputy \f28 \uc2 \f2 William\par Ruto\f28 \uc2 \f2 , whose side of the ruling Jubilee party Rotich belongs to.\par     Investors have also been concerned about a potential drop in\par export earnings from key commodities like tea and the tourism\par business. Falling imports, however, mean the current account\par deficit will still improve this year, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  says.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief, Patrick Njoroge, who was sanguine\par about the shilling's weakness last week, might have changed his\par stance this week due to the technical charts, which show a drop\par below 104.60 for the shilling could unleash further weakness,\par market participants said.  \par     The shilling plunged to its lowest ever in 2011 when it hit\par 107 per dollar, mainly due to policymakers' refusal to raise\par rates in the face of high inflation. \par                ...........................Shilling spot rates\par                   .....................Shilling forward rates\par                            .......................Cross rates\par  