\par\par \b \uc2 WEEKAHEAD-AFRICA- \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Kenyan, Tanzanian shillings seen firm, Ugandan shilling unchanged\b0\par\par\uc2 410 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juni 2019\par 13:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 NAIROBI, June 6 (Reuters) - The Kenyan and Tanzanian shillings are expected to strengthen next week, while the Ugandan shilling should hold steady.\par \par \uc2 KENYA\par \par \uc2 The Kenyan shilling is seen strengthening against the dollar next week due to weak dollar demand from oil importers, with \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  still ample, traders said.\par \par \uc2 Commercial banks quoted the shilling at 101.30/50 per dollar, the same as last Thursday's close.\par \par \uc2 "The level of reserves indicates the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2  has the necessary muscle to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in case of increased volatility," a senior trader from one commercial bank told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 In March, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Kenya\uc2  said its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves were at an all-time high of $10.06 billion, or 6.4 months of import cover, thanks to a $2.1 billion Eurobond the government sold earlier that month.\par \par \uc2 TANZANIA\par \par \uc2 The Tanzanian shilling is expected to hold steady next week with a high possibility of appreciation due to dollar inflows from the mining, agriculture and tourism sectors, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The shilling was stable on Thursday at 2,293/2,303, underpinned by low dollar demand as companies met their month-end obligations.\par \par \uc2 "We expect to see the shilling remain stable next week with a high possibility of appreciating to 2,290/2,300 levels, as corporate clients will be returning to the market after holidays and (on) inflows from mining, agriculture and tourism," a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader from a Dar es Salaam commercial bank told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 UGANDA\par \par \uc2 The Ugandan shilling is seen trading rangebound ahead of a budget reading for the 2019/2020 fiscal year, with most players keeping to the sidelines until the new budget is unveiled.\par \par \uc2 At 0946 GMT commercial banks quoted the shilling at 3,762/3,772 compared to last Thursday's close at 3,755/3,765.\par \par \uc2 A trader at a commercial bank in the capital Kampala said the shilling would trade in a 3,750-3,780 range in the period before a budget reading scheduled for June 13.\par \par \uc2 "There's some uncertainly regarding what might come out in the budget, so I think we'll see demand remain flat until after (that)," the trader said. (Reporting by John Ndiso in Nairobi, Elias Biryabarema in Kampala and Nuzulack Dausen in Dar es Salaam; Compiled by Clement Uwiringiyimana; Editing by Jan Harvey)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-6-9T11:30:39.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020190606ef6601ua5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
