\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Kenya says \uc2 IMF\uc2  stand-by arrangement over, still engaging with the fund\b0\par\par\uc2 494 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 September 2018\par 14:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Stand-by arrangement was first secured in 2016\par \par \uc2 * Finance minister says programme not unusual (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reaction, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 By George Obulutsa\par \par \uc2 NAIROBI, Sept 13 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stand-by loan deal with the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  has expired but the country will continue to talk to the Fund about what funding facilities it can access in future, Finance Minister \uc2 Henry Rotich\uc2  said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Kenya had secured a six-month extension in March of the $989.8 million arrangement, agreed in 2016 to help cushion the economy in case of unforeseen external shocks that could upset the balance of payments. It included a stand-by credit facility of $494.9 million that expired in March.\par \par \uc2 No funds were ever drawn down.\par \par \uc2 Rotich told reporters the expiration of the programme was not unusual, since Kenya has had more than a dozen such programmes over the last 15 years that came and went.\par \par \uc2 "There is nothing unique about any programme ending. I think what's important is that we did have a very successful two-year programme, which is now coming to an end," he told reporters after a meeting on the budget.\par \par \uc2 The shilling weakened by as much as 0.3 percent from Wednesday's close after news of the expiry of the facility with \uc2 IMF\uc2 , forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the sale of dollars to banks in the afternoon.\par \par \uc2 Talks with the Washington-based fund were now focusing on the next type of facility the country can secure, Rotich said.\par \par \uc2 When Reuters contacted its local office, the \uc2 IMF\uc2  said it would comment later.\par \par \uc2 Rotich said East Africa's biggest economy should wean itself off support from the \uc2 IMF\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "As a country that is entering into the medium and developed countries, we should be relying less and less on \uc2 IMF\uc2  facilities, especially if you have come of age in our macroeconomic management," he said.\par \par \uc2 "But we can still engage and get back to it if we feel it is still necessary. We will continue to engage with the fund going forward, the way we have done it in the past."\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 IMF\uc2  had set conditions for extending the stand-by arrangement, including the repeal of a cap on commercial lending rates which was imposed in 2016.\par \par \uc2 Rotich tried to repeal the cap in his June budget, but parliament voted to keep the upper limit of the rate cap while getting rid of a minimum deposit rate it had previously imposed.\par \par \uc2 Kamau Thugge\uc2 , the principal secretary to the \b \highlight22\uc2 ministry of finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , had earlier told the budget meeting that not having an \uc2 IMF\uc2  precautionary arrangement would not hurt the economy.\par \par \uc2 The economy was expected to grow 6.2 percent in 2019, up from a forecast 6.0 percent this year, Thugge said in a presentation. (Editing by Duncan Miriri and Matthew Mpoke Bigg) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-9-13T13:26:02.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180913ee9d019g5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
