\par\par \b \uc2 African Markets - Factors to watch on June 8\b0\par\par\uc2 484 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juni 2018\par 07:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The following company announcements, scheduled economic indicators, debt and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market\par moves and political events may affect African markets on Friday.\par     - - - - -\par  GLOBAL MARKETS\par  Asian shares stepped back from a 2-1/2 month high on Friday\par  as risk appetite soured on bets that Europe's massive\par  monetary stimulus was nearing an end, compounded by\par  uncertainty over trade relations ahead of a key meeting of\par  global leaders.\par             \par  \par  WORLD OIL PRICES\par  Oil prices were stable on Friday, supported by Venezuela's\par  struggles to meet its supply obligations and by ongoing\par  output cuts led by producer cartel \f28 \uc2 \f2 OPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2 , although surging\par  U.S. crude output was looming over markets.\par       \par  \par  EMERGING MARKETS\par  For the top emerging markets news, double click on\par             \par  \par  AFRICA STOCKS\par  For the latest news on African stocks, click on     \par  \par  AFRICA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par  Uganda's shilling is forecast to weaken on expected demand\par  from commercial banks and importers, fuelled by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par  bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's lack of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , while Ghana, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Kenya\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and\par  Tanzania's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are expected to remain steady.\par              \par  \par  SOUTH AFRICA MARKETS\par  South Africa's rand sunk to its weakest level in more than\par  five months on Thursday as sentiment toward the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was\par  soured by a combination of poor economic growth and\par  investors fleeing emerging markets.\par              \par  \par  NIGERIA MARKETS\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nigeria's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will start to auction the Chinese\par  yuan within the next month at an exchange rate to be set via\par  book building, an official said on Thursday, in an attempt\par  to reduce its reliance on the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for imports from\par  Asia.\par              \par  \par  KENYA MARKETS\par  The Kenyan shilling KES= strengthened slightly against the\par  dollar on Thursday with some support from hard \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par  sent in from its nationals who live abroad, traders said.\par                 \par  \par  KENYA CORRUPTION\par  A Kenyan parliamentary committee has cut funding for the\par  state-run National Youth Service (NYS) after two corruption\par  scandals there, the committee's chairman said on Thursday.\par                   \par  \par  GHANA MARKETS\par  Ghana sold 477.6 million cedis ($101.6 mln) worth of a fresh\par  10-year domestic \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bond on Thursday and will pay a\par  yield of 17.5 percent, transaction arrangers said.\par              \par  \par  GHANA FOOTBALL\par  Ghana has decided to dissolve its national football\par  association a day after officials, including the body's\par  president, were shown in a documentary taking kickbacks, the\par  information minister said on Thursday.\par              \par  \par  ZIMBABWE OPPOSITION\par  Zimbabwe's main opposition party promised on Thursday to\par  revive the economy if it wins an election in July by cutting\par  taxes, abolishing a quasi-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  "bond note", joining a\par  regional monetary union and seeking debt relief.\par              \par  \par  BURUNDI PRESIDENT\par  Burundi's long-serving President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Pierre Nkurunziza\f28 \uc2 \f2  promised\par  on Thursday to step down when his term ends in 2020, easing\par  fears of fresh violence in the impoverished country.\par                  \par  \par      For the latest precious metals report click on        \par      For the latest base metals report click on         \par      For the latest crude oil report click on\f28 \par \par \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-6-8T06:11:44.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180608ee68007vd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
