\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW-Kenya faces high political uncertainty but institutions stronger -CenBank Gov\b0\par\par\uc2 632 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 2017\par 16:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Uncertainty high over repeat vote\par \par \uc2 * Kenyans like "noisy politics" says Njoroge\par \par \uc2 * Committed to flexible exchange rate policy (adds quotes, data, background)\par \par \uc2 By Karin Strohecker\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Oct 18 (Reuters) - Political uncertainty is high in Kenya following the annulment of the August presidential elections, but political and judicial institutions have emerged stronger in the process, the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Opposition leader \uc2 Raila Odinga\uc2  was due to face President \uc2 Uhuru Kenyatta\uc2  on Oct. 26 in a repeat of the presidential vote held in August which was annulled by the Supreme Court on procedural irregularities.\par \par \uc2 But Odinga withdrew last week, throwing East Africa's largest economy - a stable Western ally in a tumultuous region - deeper into uncertainty. The head of the election commission said on Wednesday it would be "difficult" to guarantee a free and fair repeat vote.\par \par \uc2 "The current state of affairs is one of high uncertainty, but I think the point here is that it is all political uncertainty, based on recent announcements by the Supreme Court and the sequence of events that followed that," \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Patrick Njoroge told Reuters in an interview.\par \par \uc2 "I see it as a mark of maturity of the democratic process," he added.\par \par \uc2 Kenyans liked "noisy politics" Njoroge said, adding he saw some signs of delays when it came to government spending on big projects. However, this was not excessive and the government was still functioning, he added.\par \par \uc2 "Kenya is very resilient, and the dynamics we have seen so far underscore Kenya's resilience," he said. "We know two things for sure \u8211\'20\'13 whoever wins will be a Kenyan, and whoever wins will be supporting market-based policies."\par \par \uc2 Asked about the economic impact of the current situation, Njoroge said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in the process of revising down its growth forecast.\par \par \uc2 "Some of this will shave a bit off growth, and some of this will be (government investment) decisions that have been delayed ... but bear in mind that the government has continued to function," he said.\par \par \uc2 "We still think there isn't a precipitous collapse in growth, on the contrary we still believe that we will have growth rates above 5 percent," he said, speaking on the sidelines of a FT Live conference.\par \par \uc2 "VERY LITTLE \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 "\par \par \uc2 Statistics released in September showed that \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy grew 5.0 percent in the second quarter of the year - a slower expansion than the previous year due to a weaker performance in agriculture, manufacturing and financial services.\par \par \uc2 Asked about the performance of the Kenyan shilling, Njoroge said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was committed to the flexible exchange rate policy, but had smoothened out excess volatility.\par \par \uc2 "We have not been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in any market way - in that matter we have not deviated from our flexible exchange rate policy, only smoothing out excess volatility as we see it."\par \par \uc2 The scale on which the bank had done so was "very, very little" he said, declining to give further numbers.\par \par \uc2 "It happens, let's say, once every couple of weeks - if at all."\par \par \uc2 According to traders, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sold dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market earlier on Wednesday after the shilling weakened on news that an election official had resigned her job a week before the repeat election.\par \par \uc2 While the shilling has come under some pressure now and then, it has stayed fairly rangebound since mid-August, with market participants pointing to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Njoroge said the stability of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was down to the country's improving, balanced current account. The shilling has weakened less than one percent against the dollar since the start of the year. (Reporting by Karin Strohecker; Editing by Jeremy Gaunt and Andrew Heavens) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-10-18T15:46:12.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020171018edai00l8b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
