\par\par \b \uc2 African Markets - Factors to watch on Dec 18\b0\par\par\uc2 455 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 2015\par 06:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par NAIROBI, Dec 18 (Reuters) - The following company\par announcements, scheduled economic indicators, debt and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par market moves and political events may affect African markets on\par Friday.\par     - - - - -\par  GLOBAL MARKETS\par  Asian shares took their cue from Wall Street and slipped on\par  Friday, and Japanese stocks returned to negative territory\par  after briefly jumping on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's statement that\par  it would expand parts of its stimulus programme.            \par  \par  WORLD OIL PRICES\par  Crude futures were mixed in Asian trading on Friday as fresh\par  signs of inventory building and the Federal Reserves rate\par  hike this week kept prices under pressure amid a global glut\par  of oil that shows no sign of abating.      \par  \par  EMERGING MARKETS\par  For the top emerging markets news, double click on\par             \par  \par  AFRICA STOCKS\par  For the latest news on African stocks, click on     \par  \par  SOUTH AFRICA\par  South African stocks rose to a more than one-week high on\par  Thursday after the United States raised interest rates for\par  the first time in nearly a decade, but a stronger dollar\par  weighed on the battered rand.             \par  \par  NIGERIA MARKETS\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nigeria's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  advised commercial banks to limit how\par  much customers can spend abroad using their debits cards,\par  two executives said on Thursday, in the latest crackdown on\par  dollar demand to save its dwindling foreign reserves.\par              \par  \par  NIGERIA OIL\par  Nigeria is producing 2.1 million barrels of oil per day\par  (bpd) and aims to boost output to 2.4 million next year, the\par  head of state oil firm NNPC said on Thursday.             \par  \par  KENYA MARKETS\par  Kenya's shilling KES= was steady on Thursday, hovering near\par  the level of 102.50 to the dollar where the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in recent weeks. Shares\par  slipped.       \par  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 KENYA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ECONOMY\par  The \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  trimmed its forecast for\par  Kenya's economic growth on Wednesday, projecting gross\par  domestic product would expand about 6 percent next year\par  after growing a less-than-expected 5.6 percent in 2015.\par                 \par  \par  IVORY COAST\par  Ivory Coast has become eligible for a 300 billion CFA franc\par  ($500 million) grant from U.S. foreign aid agency the\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Millennium Challenge Corporation (MCC)\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Prime Minister\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Daniel Kablan Duncan\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on Thursday.             \par  \par  ANGOLA INFLATION\par  Angola's consumer inflation quickened to 13.29 percent\par  year-on-year in November from 12.40 in October, data posted\par  on the statistics office website showed on Thursday.\par              \par  \par  NIGER COUP ATTEMPT\par  Niger's government has foiled an attempted coup and arrested\par  people who planned to use aerial firepower to seize control,\par  President Mahamadou Issoufou said on national television on\par  Thursday.             \par  \par  \par      For the latest precious metals report click on        \par      For the latest base metals report click on         \par      For the latest crude oil report click on       \par   \par   \par \par  