\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Kenya  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  to hold interest rate at 11.5 percent on Nov.17\b0\par\par\uc2 332 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 November 2015\par 16:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Kenya\uc2  to hold benchmark rate on Tuesday\par \par \uc2 * Rate to be left at 11.5 percent\par \par \uc2 * For poll forecasts: reuters://realtime/verb=Open/url=cpurl://apps.cp./Apps/cb-polls?RIC=KECBIR%3DECI\par \par \uc2 By Vuyani Ndaba\par \par \uc2 JOHANNESBURG, Nov 16 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Kenya\uc2  will keep its benchmark interest rate unchanged at 11.5 percent on Tuesday, having already raised borrowing costs by 300 basis points this year to ward off inflationary pressures, a Reuters poll found.\par \par \uc2 Only two of 10 analysts polled in the past week expected a hike in rates this month, ahead of an expected \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  rate increase that is likely to put emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  under increased pressure.\par \par \uc2 Central banks in emerging markets have acted to stem falls in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid rising concerns over the health of the global economy and a tumble in commodity prices.\par \par \uc2 "The interest rate hikes were front-loaded in the current tightening cycle. Monetary policy has done all it can at this point, any further adjustment will come down to the fiscal authorities," said Alan Cameron, economist at Exotix in London.\par \par \uc2 In recent weeks, \uc2 Kenya's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has used a mixture of shilling mop-up \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  and dollar sales to support the weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has been hit by global dollar strength and Kenya's widening trade gap and hefty budget deficit.\par \par \uc2 Kenya's shilling has recovered from its weakest level this year of 106.6 per dollar in early September to around 102.3.\par \par \uc2 "The retracement in the shilling means that Kenyan inflation will now peak at a lower level," said Razia Khan, head of Africa research at \uc2 Standard Chartered\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Patrick Njoroge has said tight liquidity in \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2 's money market and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  have stabilised the shilling and prices, helping ensure sustainable growth. (Editing by Catherine Evans)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-11-19T15:44:51.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020151116ebbg00lre\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
