\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Kenyan shilling steady after c.bank sells dollars; stocks fall\b0\par\par\uc2 344 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 2015\par 15:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Adds \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , market closer data)\par     NAIROBI, Nov 10 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Kenya\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's shilling closed\par flat on Tuesday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold dollars to support\par the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for the second day in a row.\par     At 1330 GMT market close, the shilling was quoted at\par 102.25/35 to the dollar, unchanged from Monday's close.\par     One Nairobi-based trader said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at\par least three times during the day, selling small quantities of\par dollars to keep the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pegged on the strong side of\par 102.50.\par     "They are sending a sign to the market that they will defend\par the 102.50 level," said the trader.\par     Earlier in the day traders reported dollar demand from\par energy firms and general importers. The shilling was also hurt\par by falling yields on government debt, which is reducing offshore\par investor appetite for the paper. \par     The shilling, down about 13 percent against the dollar this\par year, has recently been supported by inflows of dollars from\par offshore investors chasing high-yielding government debt. But\par yields tumbled last week.\par     The yield on 91-day paper slid below 14 percent from nearly\par 20 percent a week before.\par     On the equity market, the NSE 20 share index inched\par down 5.31 points, or 0.1 percent, to close at 3,887.53 points.\par     In the debt market, bonds worth 1.43 billion shillings ($14\par million) were traded, compared with the previous session's 1.37\par billion shillings.\par     \par     \par                ...........................Shilling spot rates \par                   .....................Shilling forward rates \par                            .......................Cross rates \par          ..................................Local contributors \par            .......................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Kenya Index \par           .....................Kenyan Bonds contributor pages \par                           \f28 \uc2 \f2 ...............Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  bill yields \par         ..................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par         .........................Horizontal repo transactions \par          ,       ................Daily interbank lending rate \par               .............................Kenya Bond pricing \par              ..................Real time Africa economic data \par  <ECI & AFR> ...........................African economic news\par           .................................NSE-20 Share Index\par          .................................NSE All Share Index\par              ...........................FT NSE Kenya 15 Index\par              .......................... FT NSE Kenya 25 Index\par   SPEED GUIDES:\par                                     \par             \par  ($1 = 102.1500 Kenyan shillings)\par \par  (Writing by Edmund Blair, Drazen Jorgic; editing by John\par Stonestreet)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-11-10T15:20:19.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020151110ebba00hrr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
