\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-\uc2 Kenya's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  chief says shilling stabilised\b0\par\par\uc2 478 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 2015\par 12:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 * Governor promises to improve banking supervision\par \par \uc2 * Fraud at mid-sized bank rattled market\par \par \uc2 * Investors seen more confident in govt borrowing plan (Adds comment on falling commercial lending rates)\par \par \uc2 By Duncan Miriri\par \par \uc2 NAIROBI, Nov 10 (Reuters) - Tight liquidity in \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2 's money market and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  have stabilised the shilling and prices, helping ensure sustainable growth, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Patrick Njoroge said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 He also told a senate committee that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would improve banking supervision after mid-sized lender Imperial Bank was taken into receivership last month, rattling investors and the public. The receiver later confirmed substantial fraud at the privately owned bank.\par \par \uc2 "Price stability will provide the necessary environment for a sustainable growth in the long term," Njoroge said.\par \par \uc2 In recent weeks, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has used a mixture of shilling mop-up \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  and dollar sales to support the weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has been hit by global dollar strength, Kenya's widening trade gap and a hefty budget deficit.\par \par \uc2 "The tight liquidity conditions experienced in September and October have eased, as reflected in the decline in the interbank rates," Njoroge said, adding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had no plans to start another tightening cycle.\par \par \uc2 Interbank rates have fallen and yields on \uc2 Treasury\uc2  bills tumbled last week after climbing above 20 percent. The shilling, now about 11 percent weaker since the start of the year, has risen off its September lows.\par \par \uc2 The governor said investors were confident the government was "on top of its borrowing plan ... In that sense there is much more credibility in terms of interest rates remaining where they are".\par \par \uc2 He said easing government debt rates would help bring commercial bank lending rates down: "We believe that (commercial) interest rates will also come down quite soon. We are not talking months, we are talking weeks, even."\par \par \uc2 When Imperial Bank was taken into receivership, tight liquidity conditions exacerbated challenges for smaller banks seeking funds, although that issue eased when it became clear that the fraud was not a systemic banking issue.\par \par \uc2 Njoroge said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would increase the numbers of supervision staff and their skills. He also said reopening Imperial Bank, which the receiver has said is still viable, would boost public confidence, but did not give a timeline.\par \par \uc2 To avoid a funding squeeze for smaller banks in future, he said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would encourage sharing liquidity in the market, which he said was "lopsided" towards four big banks.\par \par \uc2 He did not name them, but the biggest Kenyan banks include \uc2 Kenya Commercial Bank\uc2  and Equity Bank.\par \par \uc2 Fraudulent withdrawals and other illegal transactions at Imperial Bank amounted to more than 34 billion shillings ($333 million) over 13 years, the receiver said.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 102.2500 Kenyan shillings) (Writing by Edmund Blair; Editing by Catherine Evans) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-11-10T12:40:35.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020151110ebba00ba2