\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Kenyan shilling flat after  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  sells dollars; shares rise\b0\par\par\uc2 376 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 November 2015\par 15:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Adds \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , closing market data)\par     NAIROBI, Nov 9 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Kenya\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's shilling closed\par flat on Monday after a day of volatile trading which prompted\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to sell dollars to support the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     At 1330 GMT market close, the shilling was quoted at\par 102.25/35 to the dollar, unchanged from Friday's close.\par     One Nairobi-based trader said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Kenya\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par (CBK) \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market when the shilling rapidly\par weakened to 102.60/70 and then continued \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for "the\par better part of the day".\par     "We have a lot of dollar demand from manufacturing and\par energy sectors, so there is still expectation the shilling will\par continue to weaken" in coming days, the trader said.   \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said in a weekly report that it had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves of $6.9 billion as of Nov. 5, up from $6.1\par billion at the start of October.\par     "That will put the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in a good position to\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if they want to protect the local unit," a dealer at a\par commercial bank said earlier in the day.\par     The shilling has recently been helped by offshore investors\par selling dollars to buy high-yielding government debt. T-bills\par yields tumbled last week. The yield on 91-day paper slid below\par 14 percent from nearly 20 percent a week before. \par     On the equity market, the NSE 20 share index rose\par 20.27 points, or 0.5 percent, to close at 3,892.84 points.\par     In the debt market, bonds worth 1.3 billion shillings \par ($12.7 million) were traded, compared with the previous\par session's 458 million shillings.\par     \par                ...........................Shilling spot rates \par                   .....................Shilling forward rates \par                            .......................Cross rates \par          ..................................Local contributors \par            .......................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Kenya Index \par           .....................Kenyan Bonds contributor pages \par                           \f28 \uc2 \f2 ...............Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  bill yields \par         ..................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par         .........................Horizontal repo transactions \par          ,       ................Daily interbank lending rate \par               .............................Kenya Bond pricing \par              ..................Real time Africa economic data \par  <ECI & AFR> ...........................African economic news\par           .................................NSE-20 Share Index\par          .................................NSE All Share Index\par              ...........................FT NSE Kenya 15 Index\par              ...............