\par\par \b \uc2 Kenya shilling firms versus dollar, tight liquidity helps\b0\par\par\uc2 312 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 September 2015\par 10:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par NAIROBI, Sept 11 (Reuters) - Kenya's shilling firmed\par a touch on Friday with dollar demand from energy and\par telecommunications firms offset by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's injection of\par greenbacks into the market, and tight liquidity. \par     At 0800 GMT, commercial banks quoted the shilling at\par 105.25/35 to the dollar against Thursday's close of 105.40/50.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Kenya\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market on Monday and\par Tuesday, selling substantial quantities of dollars to boost the\par shilling as the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  edged closer to its record low of\par 106.80, set in October 2011. \par     "Right now, there is little activity on trade so far this\par morning. Both demand and supply seems matched at this level,"\par said a trader at one Nairobi-based commercial bank. \par     "What could also be containing it at this level is because\par liquidity seems to have now reduced," he added.\par     Traders said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's sale of dollars has stemmed\par shilling losses, for now, and expect the threat of further\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weigh on the minds of market players.\par     The shilling, down about 13.7 percent against the dollar\par this year, has come under pressure from a broad rally in the\par dollar, Kenya's large current account deficit and weak foreign\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  inflows from tourism after a number of attacks by\par Somalia's \f28 \uc2 \f2 al Shabaab\f28 \uc2 \f2  insurgents.\par                ...........................Shilling spot rates \par                   .....................Shilling forward rates \par                            .......................Cross rates \par          ..................................Local contributors \par            \f28 \uc2 \f2 .......................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Kenya\f28 \uc2 \f2  Index \par           .....................Kenyan Bonds contributor pages \par                           \f28 \uc2 \f2 ...............Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  bill yields \par         ..................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par         .........................Horizontal repo transactions \par          ,       ................Daily interbank lending rate \par               .............................Kenya Bond pricing \par              ..................Real time Africa economic data \par  <ECI & AFR> ...........................African economic news\par           .................................NSE-20 Share Index\par          .................................NSE All Share Index\par              ...........................FT NSE Kenya 15 Index\par              .......................... FT NSE Kenya 25 Index\par   SPEED GUIDES:\par                                     \par             \par  \par  (Reporting by Aaron Maasho; Editing by George Obulutsa)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-9-11T09:33:56.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150911eb9b008lc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
