\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Kenya's shilling steady against dollar, stocks slightly lower\b0\par\par\uc2 396 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 2015\par 16:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Threat of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  action supporting the shilling\par     * Benchmark NSE20 index nudges slightly lower\par \par  (Adds trader comment)\par     NAIROBI, Sept 10 (Reuters) - Kenya's shilling was little\par changed against the dollar on Thursday, with dollar demand from\par the telecoms sector offsetting the impact of two \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  earlier in the week.\par     At the close of trade at 1330 GMT, commercial banks quoted\par the shilling at 105.40/50, barely changed on Wednesday's close\par of 105.35/50.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Kenya\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market on Monday and\par Tuesday, selling substantial quantities of dollars to boost the\par shilling as the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  edged closer to its record low of\par 106.80, set in October 2011. \par     "Today has been thin on volumes but a few companies from the\par telecoms sector were buying (dollars)," said a trader at one\par Nairobi-based commercial bank. It was not immediately clear why\par the telecoms firms were buying.\par     Traders say the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's sale of dollars has stemmed\par shilling losses, for now, and expect the threat of further\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weigh on the minds of market players.\par     "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  came in a big way, and after such an\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  people are usually cautious," added the trader.\par     The shilling, down about 16.5 percent against the dollar\par this year, has come under pressure from a broad rally in the\par dollar, Kenya's large current account deficit and weak foreign\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  inflows from tourism after a number of attacks by\par Somalia's \f28 \uc2 \f2 al Shabaab\f28 \uc2 \f2  insurgents.\par     The benchmark NSE20 share index was barely changed,\par drifting 2.11 points lower to close at 4,217.78 points.\par     On the secondary market, government bonds valued at 687\par million shillings  ($6.52 million) were traded, down from 1.1\par billion the previous day.\par     \par     \par     \par                ...........................Shilling spot rates\par                   .....................Shilling forward rates\par                            .......................Cross rates\par          ..................................Local contributors\par            \f28 \uc2 \f2 .......................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Kenya\f28 \uc2 \f2  Index\par           .....................Kenyan Bonds contributor pages\par                           \f28 \uc2 \f2 ...............Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  bill yields\par         ..................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par         .........................Horizontal repo transactions\par          ,       ................Daily interbank lending rate\par               .............................Kenya Bond pricing\par              ..................Real time Africa economic data\par  <ECI & AFR> ...........................African economic new