\par\par \b \uc2 African Markets - Factors to watch on April 9\b0\par\par\uc2 516 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 2015\par 06:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par NAIROBI, April 9 (Reuters) - The following company announcements, scheduled economic\par indicators, debt and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market moves and political events may affect African markets on\par Thursday.\par     - - - - -\par  EVENTS:\par  *\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Kenya\f28 \uc2 \f2  to auction 91-day Treasury bills worth a total 1 billion\par  shillings.\par  \par  GLOBAL MARKETS\par  Asian stocks rose on Thursday, extending the previous session's gains, while the\par  dollar drew support from minutes of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 's last meeting showing the\par  U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was still on course to hike interest rates this year.\par                            \par  \par  WORLD OIL PRICES\par  Oil prices rose more than a percent on Thursday, clawing back a part of the 6 percent\par  slump in the previous session that was triggered by a shock jump in U.S. crude\par  inventories and record Saudi output, although analysts said sentiment remained\par  bearish.                     \par  \par  EMERGING MARKETS\par  For the top emerging markets news, double click on            \par  \par  AFRICA STOCKS\par  For the latest news on African stocks, click on     \par  \par  SOUTH AFRICA MARKETS\par  South Africa's rand held its ground against the dollar on Wednesday, tracking\par  generally firmer emerging markets after investors bet that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  could\par  signal a slower than expected pace in raising U.S. rates.               \par      Stocks rose for the second consecutive day on Wednesday as investors scooped up\par  shares in blue-chip heavy-weight \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kumba Iron Ore\f28 \uc2 \f2           as the price of the commodity\par  steadied.               \par  \par  NIGERIA MARKETS\par  Nigeria's main share index fell on Wednesday for the second consecutive day, dropping\par  by 2.6 percent in early trade on profit taking after surging last week following a\par  peaceful presidential vote, traders said.               \par  \par  NIGERIA TRANSCORP RESULTS\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Transnational Corp. of Nigeria\f28 \uc2 \f2 , a conglomerate with interest in hotels, power and oil\par  and gas, said on Wednesday its 2014 pretax profit fell 14 percent to 7.73 billion\par  naira ($39 million) from year ago.               \par  \par  KENYA MARKETS\par  The Kenyan shilling        eased on Wednesday but remained within its recent ranges as\par  market players traded cautiously wary of another \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par                 \par  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 KENYA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SECURITY\par  Political pressure mounted on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Kenya\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's president on Wednesday with scathing editorials\par  and growing anger at a seven hour delay in the deployment of a special forces unit\par  that eventually ended the bloody siege at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Garissa University\f28 \uc2 \f2  last week.\par                 \par  \par  UGANDA LENDING RATE\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Uganda's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  raised its benchmark lending rate              for the first\par  time since June 2014 to forestall a rise in core inflation caused by a weakening local\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and faster economic growth.                \par  \par  IVORY COAST COCOA\par  Ivory Coast will allocate half of this year's cocoa mid-crop to local grinders and is\par  working on the details of tax breaks to take effect in the 2015-2016 season in a bid\par  to stimulate the sector, government and industry sources said on Wednesday.\par                 \par  \par  ZAMBIA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par  Zambia's kwacha        strengthened over 1 percent against the dollar on Wednesday as\par  the market anticipated changes to the existing tax regime in favour of mining\par  companies.                \par  \par      For the latest precious metals report click on        \par      For the latest base metals report click on         \par      For the latest crude oil report click on\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-4-9T05:36:02.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150409eb49005k2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
