\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Kenyan shilling flat as caution sets in, shares fall\b0\par\par\uc2 415 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2015\par 15:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Updates with closing rate, shares)\par     NAIROBI, March 17 (Reuters) - Kenya's shilling was\par steady at near 3-year lows on Tuesday, as traders acted\par carefully on prospects of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pumping in dollars to\par cut any volatility.\par     The benchmark shares index fell on profit-taking.\par     The shilling closed trade at 92.05/15 against the dollar,\par unchanged from Monday's close. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold an\par undisclosed amount of dollars on Monday when the shilling\par touched its lowest level since Nov. 2011.\par     "We were largely unchanged as market players now take\par caution owing to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Kenya\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,"\par said a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader at a leading commercial bank. \par     Traders who build long dollar positions usually get caught\par out if the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  firms after a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Concerns about further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were deepened by similar\par action in neighbouring Uganda where the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold\par dollars on Monday to prop up the Ugandan shilling after\par it slid, said the trader. \par     The Kenyan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has fared better than the Ugandan one\par this year, losing 1.83 percent against the greenback compared\par with a 4.66 percent fall for the Ugandan shilling.\par     The drops have partly been driven by a globally firmer\par dollar on expectation the U.S. Federal Reserve would hike rates\par faster than expected.\par     In the stock market, the benchmark NSE-20 share index\par  fell 0.5 percent to close at 5,313.84 points, driven by\par profit-taking especially by investors abroad.\par     "Foreign investors were net sellers and they have been\par sellers for quite a while," said Stella Wambugu, a research\par analyst at Standard Investment Bank.\par     The index has risen just once in the past ten sessions as\par investors started booking gains after it hit a seven-year peak.\par     In the debt market, bonds worth 779 million shillings \par ($8.47 million) were traded, down from Monday's volume of 1.4\par billion shillings.\par                ...........................Shilling spot rates \par                   .....................Shilling forward rates \par                            .......................Cross rates \par          ..................................Local contributors \par            \f28 \uc2 \f2 .......................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Kenya\f28 \uc2 \f2  Index \par           .....................Kenyan Bonds contributor pages \par                           ...............Treasury bill yields \par         ..................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par         .........................Horizontal repo transactions \par          ,       ................Daily interbank lending rate \par               .............................Kenya Bond pricing \par              ..................Real time Africa economic data \par  <ECI & A