\par\par \b \uc2 Kenyan shilling hovers around more than three-year lows\b0\par\par\uc2 281 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 2015\par 08:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par NAIROBI, Jan 8 (Reuters) - Kenya's shilling hovered\par around its weakest level in more than three years on Thursday\par amid continuing corporate demand for dollars.\par     By 0708 GMT, the shilling was trading at 91.05/25 to the\par dollar, little changed from Wednesday's close of 91.10/20.\par     "There is persistent demand with a bit of jitters now we are\par trading above 91.00," said Duncan Kinuthia, head of trading at\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commercial Bank of Africa\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "In the absence of any action by the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , I guess we are going to gravitate towards 91.50."\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Kenya\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on several\par occasions in recent weeks by selling dollars to the support the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  but the sales have only slowed a steady decline in the\par shilling.\par     A spate of militant attacks has hurt the flow of tourist\par dollars, a major source of revenues for the east African nation,\par helping drive the shilling lower during 2014.\par     "Whatever supply (of dollars) comes in will just stall the\par trend. The trend is basically for a weaker shilling," said\par another trader, who asked not to be identified.\par     \par                ...........................Shilling spot rates\par                   .....................Shilling forward rates\par                            .......................Cross rates\par          .................................