\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Kenya shilling weakens, top shares inch up\b0\par\par\uc2 398 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 2015\par 15:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Importer dollar demand weighs on shilling\par     * Blue chip share index edges up in correction\par \par  (Adds closing rate, shares)\par     By Duncan Miriri\par     NAIROBI, Jan 6 (Reuters) - Kenya's shilling weakened\par on Tuesday, weighed down by corporate demand for dollars, while\par the benchmark share index eked out meagre gains as investors\par regrouped following losses in the previous session.\par     At the 1300 GMT close of trade, leading commercial banks\par posted the shilling at 90.90/91.00, lower than Monday's close of\par 90.80/90.\par     The Kenyan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened late on Monday as importers\par resumed business after the holidays.\par     "Dollar demand from yesterday persisted today and it is\par specifically from the oil sector," said Nahashon Mungai, a\par trader at \f28 \uc2 \f2 KCB Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "The market looks poised to breach the\par 91.000 level barring any \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the CBK (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Kenya\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 )."\par     The shilling weakened steadily last year in part because of\par a downturn in tourism following a series of Islamist militant\par attacks. Tourists are a major source of dollars and other hard\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for the east African nation.\par     Sustained corporate demand for dollars, jitters across\par emerging markets and thin dollar inflows into Kenya were all\par putting pressure on the shilling, said Duncan Kinuthia, head of\par trading at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commercial Bank of Africa\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     "A breach of 91.00 could open up towards 91.50," Kinuthia\par said. "General weakness will remain. I don't see anything\par supporting a strong shilling for the time being."\par     In the stock market, the benchmark NSE-20 share index\par  edged up 0.17 percent to close at 5,098.49 points.\par     Market participants said the gains reflected a correction\par after the index dropped 0.54 percent in the previous session due\par to concerns over a new capital gains tax.\par     In the debt market, bonds worth 800 million shillings were\par traded, up from 571 million shillings that changed hands on\par Monday.\par       \par                ...........................Shilling spot rates\par                   .....................Shilling forward rates\par                            .......................Cross rates\par          ..................................Local contributors\par            \f28 \uc2 \f2 .......................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Kenya\f28 \uc2 \f2  Index\par           .....................Kenyan Bonds contributor pages\par                           ...............Treasury bill yields\par         ..................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par         .........................Horizontal repo transactions\par          ,       ................Daily interbank lending rate\par               .............................Kenya Bond pricing\par              ..................Real time Africa economic data\par  <ECI & AFR> ...........................African economic news\par           .................................NSE-20 Share Index\par          .................................NSE All Share Index\par              ...........................FT NSE Kenya 15 Index\par              .......................... FT NSE Kenya 25 I