\par\par \b \uc2 Kenyan shilling slips again despite  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 379 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 November 2014\par 07:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par NAIROBI, Nov 21 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Kenya\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's shilling was back\par near three-year lows in early trading on Friday, after\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  the\par previous day had little lasting impact.\par     By 0635 GMT, the shilling was quoted at 90.10/30, weakening\par from Thursday's close of 90.05/15.\par     Dollar sales by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Kenya\f28 \uc2 \f2  (CBK) on Thursday\par initially helped the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  firm up to 89.70/90, but it\par swiftly reversed those gains. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold dollars this\par week and the last when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traded around the 90.30\par level.\par     "I suspect that CBK would have to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again because\par there seems to have been not much effect from its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par yesterday," said Nahashon Mungai at \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Kenya\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Commercial Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     Traders said the demand for dollars was mainly coming from\par energy importers and telecoms firms. They said pressure on the\par shilling could build next week as corporate demand for the U.S.\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tended to build towards the end of the month.\par     "The supply side continues to be constrained," said one\par trader at a leading commercial bank, referring to depressed\par dollar inflows from tourism and tea, another major hard \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par earner, because of lower global tea prices.\par     "I think the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will continue to offer support but\par where it is demand driven and the weakness is gradual I think\par they will let the fundamentals play a key role," he said.\par     For now, traders said the shilling was likely to be capped\par at about 90.50.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has not set any exchange rate level and\par does not usually comment on any \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but it has said it\par has enough reserves to cushion the market against shocks.\par      \par                ...........................Shilling spot rates \par                   .....................Shilling forward rates \par                            .......................Cross rates \par          ..................................Local contributors \par            \f28 \uc2 \f2 .......................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Kenya\f28 \uc2 \f2  Index \par           .....................Kenyan Bonds contributor pages \par                           \f28 \uc2 \f2 ...............Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  bill yields \par         ..................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par         .........................Horizontal repo transactions \par          ,       ................Daily interbank lending rate \par               ......................