\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Kenya \highlight\uc2  shilling firms after  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes \highlight\uc2 , shares rise\b0\par\par\uc2 404 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 2014\par 15:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 * Shilling off 3-year lows after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  support\par \par \uc2 * Bamburi cement helps buoy stocks (Updates with shilling, stocks close)\par \par \uc2 NAIROBI, Nov 14 (Reuters) - Kenya's shilling strengthened from three-year lows on Friday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling dollars. Stocks rose.\par \par \uc2 The shilling closed at 89.90/90.0 to the dollar, compared to Thursday's close of 90.25/35 - its lowest level since November 2011.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has in the past sold dollars to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  when it touched 89.50 levels. Most traders had anticipated action when it broke through the 90 level this week.\par \par \uc2 The shilling has fallen by about 4.3 percent against the dollar this year, due to a slump in hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows from tourism following a spate of attacks by Islamic militants. Tea export inflows have been hit by a global glut. The dollar has also recently strengthened against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Martin Runo, a senior trader at \uc2 Chase Bank\uc2 , said he still expected the shilling to remain under pressure.\par \par \uc2 "The shilling has a weaker bias, there is dollar demand from the oil sector and manufacturers, while there are only minimal inflows from tourism and agriculture," Runo said.\par \par \uc2 "However, if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  persists in selling dollars, the shilling could stay below the 90-level to the dollar."\par \par \uc2 In the stock market, the benchmark NSE-20 share index rose 0.3 percent or 15.92 points to 5,139.37 points.\par \par \uc2 Among the gainers was \uc2 Bamburi Cement\uc2 , which added 2 percent to end at 149 shillings, buoyed by its plans to supply cement to big infrastructure projects, including a planned new railway, Old Mutual Securities said in a research note.\par \par \uc2 In the debt market, bonds worth 5 million shillings ($55,617) were traded, down from 940 million shillings traded the previous day.\par \par \uc2 \f2 ...........................Shilling spot rates \par  .....................Shilling forward rates \par   .......................Cross rates \par ..................................Local contributors \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 .......................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Kenya\f28 \uc2 \f2  Index \par .....................Kenyan Bonds contributor pages \par   ...............Treasury bill yields \par ..................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par .........................Horizontal repo transactions \par ,................Daily interbank lending rate \par .............................Kenya Bond pricing \par ..................Real time Africa economic data \par <ECI & AFR> ...........................African economic news\par .................................NSE-20 Share Index\par .................................NSE All Share Index\par ...........................FT NSE Kenya 15 Index\par .......................... FT NSE Kenya 25 Index\par  SPEED GUIDES:\par               \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (1 US dollar = 89.9000 Kenyan shilling) (Reporting by James Macharia) \f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-11-14T15:02:37.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA000002