\par\par \b \uc2 Kenyan shilling stays at 3-year low, seen weakening further\b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 2014\par 08:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par NAIROBI, Nov 13 (Reuters) - The Kenyan shilling was\par flat at a three-year low on Thursday, with traders expecting the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to continue weakening if the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  does not\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prop up the shilling.\par     At 0730 GMT, commercial banks posted the shilling at\par 90.05/15 to the dollar, unchanged from Wednesday's close, which\par marked its lowest level since November 2011.\par     "Not much change is expected today," said a trader at a\par major commercial bank in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Kenya\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par     "The expectation is without any \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , or other\par supply that may come into the market, we'll just see a continued\par weakening of the shilling."\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has in the past sold dollars to support the\par local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when the shilling touched 89.50 levels and most\par traders were surprised when the bank did not do the same as the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  broke through the 90 mark.\par     However, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has regularly drained excess\par liquidity from the money markets in recent months, making it\par relatively costlier to hold on to long dollar positions, which\par helps strengthen the shilling. On Wednesday it sought to mop up\par 8 billion shillings ($88.84 million) in excess liquidity.\par  \par     The shilling has weakened by about 4.1 percent against the\par dollar this year, mainly due to a slump in hard \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  inflows\par from tourism following a spate of attacks by Islamic militants.\par Inflows of dollars from tea exports have also dwindled owing to\par weaker prices caused by a global glut of the commodity.\par \par                ...........................Shilling spot rates \par                   .....................Shilling forward rates \par                            .......................Cross rates \par          ..................................Local contributors \par            \f28 \uc2 \f2 .......................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Kenya\f28 \uc2 \f2  Index \par           .....................Kenyan Bonds contributor pages \par                           \f28 \uc2 \f2 ...............Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  bill yields \par         ..................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par         .........................Horizontal repo transactions \par          ,       ................Daily interbank lending rate \par               .............................Kenya Bond pricing \par              ..................Real time Africa economic data \par  <ECI & AFR> ...........................African economic news\par           .................................NSE-20 Share Index\par          .................................NSE All Share Index\par              ...........................FT NSE Kenya 15 Index\par              .......................... FT NSE Kenya 25 Index\par   SPEED GUIDES:\par                                     \par             \par     (1 US dollar = 90.00 Kenyan shilling)\par \par \par (1 US dollar = 90.0500 Kenyan shilling)\par \par  (Repo