\par\par \b \uc2 Kenyan shilling hovers near 3-year low,  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  action eyed\b0\par\par\uc2 316 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 November 2014\par 08:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par NAIROBI, Nov 12 (Reuters) - The Kenyan shilling \par hovered near a three-year low against the dollar on Wednesday,\par with traders saying they were watching for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  action\par to drain excess liquidity from the money markets or even\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by selling dollars.\par     At 0730 GMT, commercial banks posted the shilling at\par 89.90/90.10 to the dollar, little changed from the previous\par day's close of 89.95/90.05. \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Tuesday hit an intra-day low of 90.00/90.10,\par its lowest level since November 2011.\par     "I think everyone is wondering about (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 )\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Nahashon Mungai, a trader with \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Kenya\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par Commercial Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "They typically defend the 90 level."  \par     The shilling has weakened by about 4.1 percent against the\par dollar this year, mainly due to a slump in hard \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  inflows\par from tourism following a spate of attacks by Islamic militants.\par Inflows of dollars from tea exports have also dwindled owing to\par weaker prices caused by a global glut of the commodity.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has regularly drained excess liquidity from\par the money markets in recent months, making it relatively\par costlier to hold on to long dollar positions, which should help\par strengthen the shilling.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has in the past also sold dollars to\par support the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when the shilling touched 89.50\par levels.\par \par                ...........................Shilling spot rates \par                   .....................Shilling forward rates \par                            .......................Cross rates \par          ..................................Local contributors \par            \f28 \uc2 \f2 .......................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Kenya\f28 \uc2 \f2  Index \par           .....................Kenyan Bonds contributor pages \par                           \f28 \uc2 \f2 ...............Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  bill yields \par         ..................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par         .........................Horizontal repo transactions \par          ,       ................Daily interbank lending rate \par               .............................Kenya Bond pricing \par              ..................Real time Africa economic data \par  <ECI & AFR> ...........................African economic news\par           .................................NSE-20 Share Index\par          .................................NSE All Share Index\par              ...........................FT NSE Kenya 15 Index\par              .......................... FT NSE Kenya 25 Index\par   SPEED GUIDES:\par                                     \par             \par  \par  (Editing by Edith Honan and Crispian Balmer)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-11-12T08:48:25.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141112eabc008ez\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\pi