\par\par \b \uc2 Kenya shilling under pressure again after  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  action\b0\par\par\uc2 324 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2014\par 10:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 NAIROBI, Sept 22 (Reuters) - Kenya's shilling weakened on Monday in a quiet start to the week's trading after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling dollars in the two previous sessions.\par \par \uc2 A downturn in the tourism industry, after a spate of bomb and gun attacks along the coast and in the capital this year, has hurt one of the east African country's major sources of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At 0752 GMT, the shilling was trading at 88.70/80 to the dollar, compared with Friday's close of 88.50/60.\par \par \uc2 "There definitely has been pressure on the shilling in last couple of days. (\b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has propped it up pretty well," said Nahashon Mungai, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at \uc2 Kenya Commercial Bank\uc2 . "It looks like the shilling is losing a bit of strength again this morning."\par \par \uc2 Another dealer at a Nairobi-based commercial bank also noted the modest weakening but said the market was relatively quiet in early business.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday and Friday after the shilling weakened to 89.45/55 on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "They haven't made it clear what level they are uncomfortable with but it looks like a break of 89 is something they are willing to defend," said a dealer, who asked not to be named due to the sensitivity of commenting on \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.\par \par \uc2 \f2 ...........................Shilling spot rates \par  .....................Shilling forward rates \par   .......................Cross rates \par ..................................Local contributors \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 .......................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Kenya\f28 \uc2 \f2  Index \par .....................Kenyan Bonds contributor pages \par   \f28 \uc2 \f2 ...............Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  bill yields \par ..................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par .........................Horizontal repo transactions \par ,................Daily interbank lending rate \par .............................Kenya Bond pricing \par ..................Real time Africa economic data \par <ECI & AFR> ...........................African economic news\par .................................NSE-20 Share Index\par .................................NSE All Share Index\par ...........................FT NSE Kenya 15 Index\par .......................... FT NSE Kenya 25 Index\par  SPEED GUIDES:\par               \par               \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Writing by Edmund Blair; Editing by James Macharia) \f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-9-22T09:04:37.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140922ea9m006ac\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
