\par\par \b \uc2 African Markets - Factors to watch on Sept 19\b0\par\par\uc2 724 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 2014\par 07:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par NAIROBI, Sept 19 (Reuters) - The following company announcements, scheduled economic\par indicators, debt and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market moves and political events may affect African markets on\par Friday.\par     - - - - -\par  EVENTS:\par  NIGERIA - \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nigeria's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  due to set key interest rate on\par  Friday. A Reuters poll shows the bank is likely to leave\par  monetary policy unchanged.             \par  \par  GLOBAL MARKETS\par  The British pound rose sharply after the Scottish independence\par  vote indicated Scotland would remain in the United Kingdom,\par  while Wall Street's overnight gains and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alibaba Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 's red-hot\par  initial public offering underpinned Asian shares.           \par  \par  WORLD OIL PRICES\par  Brent crude held below $98 a barrel on Friday, but was set for\par  its first weekly gain in three on the possibility of lower \f28 \uc2 \f2 OPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par  output.      \par  \par  EMERGING MARKETS\par  For the top emerging markets news, double click on            \par  \par  AFRICA STOCKS\par  For the latest news on African stocks, click on     \par  \par  AFRICA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par  The Kenyan shilling        is expected to remain under pressure\par  next week due to increased dollar demand and slowing inflows,\par  despite \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  efforts to keep its slide in check.\par              \par  \par  SOUTH AFRICA RATES    \par  South African \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gill Marcus\f28 \uc2 \f2 , a steadying\par  influence on Africa's most advanced economy during five years of\par  strikes, low growth and rising inflation, stepped down on\par  Thursday, sending the rand to its weakest level in seven months.\par              \par  \par  SOUTH AFRICA MARKETS\par      * South African stocks traded sideways on Wednesday as a\par  sharp drop by luxury goods retailer Richemont          weighed\par  on a lacklustre market waiting for direction from a key U.S.\par  Federal Reserve statement later in the day.     \par      * South Africa's rand weakened against the dollar on\par  Thursday, falling to a 7-month low after respected Reserve Bank\par  Governor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gill Marcus\f28 \uc2 \f2  said she would not renew her contract when\par  her five year term ends in November.             \par  \par  NIGERIA OIL \par      * A strike by Nigeria's oil unions is not having any\par  immediate impact on crude oil exports from Africa's top\par  exporter, despite moving into a third day, spokesmen for leading\par  operator Shell          and Nigeria LNG said.\par  \par  NIGERIA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     \par  Nigeria's naira          fell 0.12 percent on Thursday to 163.65\par  against the dollar, hit by falling global oil prices LCOc1,\par  despite a third day of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , dealers said.\par  The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  closed at 163.45.\par  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 KENYA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FINMIN ON CAPITAL GAINS TAX\par  Kenya sought to assure investors on Thursday that a 5 percent\par  capital gains tax, signed into law last week, was low enough to\par  avoid hurting the economy and would not be changed soon,\par  apparently ruling out any swift hike.             \par  \par  KENYA MARKETS    \par  The Kenyan shilling        bounced from near three-year lows on\par  Thursday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Kenya\f28 \uc2 \f2  (CBK) sold an\par  unspecified amount of dollars into the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\par  Stocks inched higher.             \par  \par  KENYA T-BILLS\par  The weighted average yield on Kenya's 91-day \f28 \uc2 \f2 Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  bills\par             edged up to 8.637 percent at auction on Thursday from\par  8.219 percent last week, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said.             \par  \par  UGANDA RAILWAY \par  Uganda is hoping to secure an $8 billion loan from China to\par  build a railway network to revamp the country's transport\par  infrastructure as it prepares to start oil production.\par              \par  \par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 IVORY COAST GOVERNMENT\f28 \uc2 \f2  DEALS  \par  Most of Ivory Coast's no-bid government deals contravene\par  regulations and should have been opened up to bidding, an audit\par  by the public procurement watchdog showed on Thursday, echoing\par  growing donor concern over the contracts.             \par  \par  ZIMBABWE SUCCESSION?\par  Soon after being shoe-horned into the top ranks of Zimbabwe's\par  ruling party, the wife of ageing leader \f28 \uc2 \f2 Robert Mugabe\f28 \uc2 \f2  has gained\par  a PhD in orphanages, seen as the latest sign that she may be\par  destined for high office.             \par  \par  CONGO POLITICS    \par  Democratic Republic of Congo's government accused Catholic\par  bishops of pandering to foreign influence on Thursday after they\par  issued an open letter opposing a possible constitutional\par  revision to let President Joseph Kabila seek a third term.\par              \par  \par  EBOLA WATCH\par  The \f28 \uc2 \f2 United Nations Security Council\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Thursday declared the\par  Ebola outbreak in West Africa a "threat to international peace\par  and security" as the death toll hit 2,630 and France became the\par  latest Western nation to step up its support.             \par  \par      For the latest precious metals report click on        \par      For the latest base metals report click on         \par      For the latest crude oil report click on       \par   \par   \par    (1 US dollar = 89.2000 Kenyan shilling)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-9-19T06:45:02.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140919ea9j003sz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
