\par\par \b \uc2 Kenyan shilling steady, seen in tight range\b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 2014\par 10:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par NAIROBI, July 22 (Reuters) - The Kenyan shilling was\par treading water against the dollar on Tuesday and looked likely\par to stay in a tight range in coming days as the market expects\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would step in to keep it from appreciating,\par traders said.\par     At 0715 GMT, commercial banks quoted the shilling at\par 87.75/85 to the dollar, unchanged from Monday's close.\par     "It's going to be range bound for now," said Andlip Nazir,\par senior trader at \f28 \uc2 \f2 I&M Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     Traders forecast a range of 87.50-88 for the next few days.\par Nazir expects an even tighter range between 87.60-90 and said\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Kenya\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is likely to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again if the\par shilling tests the 88 level.\par     "We don't see the shilling going above 88 as it's being\par protected by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," he added.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is seen wanting to keep the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par relatively stable and has recently step in to keep it from\par appreciating beyond 88 to the dollar.\par     The shilling has weakened by about 1.8 percent against the\par dollar this year as tourism, a major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  earner for\par Kenya, has been hit by a series of attacks on the country,\par blamed on Somali militant group \f28 \uc2 \f2 al Shabaab\f28 \uc2 \f2 . 