\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Kenya shilling firms as dollar demand wanes\b0\par\par\uc2 325 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juli 2014\par 16:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Adds markets close, bonds)\par     By George Obulutsa\par     NAIROBI, July 16 (Reuters) - The Kenyan shilling \par firmed against the dollar on Wednesday after demand from\par companies seeking the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  eased off once they had met\par their needs, traders said.\par     At the close of trade at 1300 GMT, commercial banks quoted\par the shilling at 87.65/75 to the dollar, compared with Tuesday's\par close of 87.75/85 and recovering from a slide to 87.80/90\par earlier in Wednesday's session.\par     "We just saw some demand easing off," said Eric Gathecha, a\par trader at \f28 \uc2 \f2 I&M Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 , adding that companies that had been seeking\par the greenback earlier this week had met their needs.\par     Oil companies had been behind much of the demand for\par dollars, helping to drive the shilling lower earlier in the\par session, traders said.\par     Traders said the shilling was unlikely to weaken below 88 to\par the dollar because at that level the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Kenya\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would\par probably \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prevent further depreciation.\par     "The 88 level is a very important level in this market.\par Because last time it hit 88 level we saw CBK come in to sell\par dollars. So market is trading cautiously," Njenga said.\par     Traders said they forecast the shilling, which has lost 1.4\par percent against the dollar so far this year, to stay in the\par 87.60-88.00 level in coming days.\par     \par                ...........................Shilling spot rates\par    