\par\par \b \uc2 African Markets - Factors to watch on June 5\b0\par\par\uc2 723 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 2014\par 07:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par NAIROBI, June 5 (Reuters) - The following company announcements, scheduled economic\par indicators, debt and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market moves and political events may affect African markets on\par Thursday.\par     - - - - -\par  EVENTS:\par  *NIGERIA -Nigeria's new \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Godwin Emefiele\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par  to hold a news conference on Thursday to outline his vision\par  for the bank.\par  *KENYA-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Kenya\f28 \uc2 \f2  auctions 91-day \f28 \uc2 \f2 Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  bills\par  worth 4 billion shillings. \par  \par  GLOBAL MARKETS\par  Asian share markets grudgingly gave ground on Thursday while\par  the euro flatlined at $1.3600, hostage to great expectations\par  that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will finally end months of\par  dithering by easing policy further.                          \par  \par  WORLD OIL PRICES\par  Brent crude slipped to a three-week low at $108 on Thursday\par  on ample supply in the United States and as tensions over\par  Ukraine cooled.                     \par  \par  EMERGING MARKETS\par  For the top emerging markets news, double click on           \par  \par  AFRICA STOCKS\par  For the latest news on African stocks, click on     \par  \par  SOUTH AFRICA MARKETS\par  South Africa's rand fell to fresh 10-week lows against the\par  U.S. dollar on Wednesday, kept on the back foot by investor\par  worries about the state of the economy and the threat of mine\par  strikes spreading to other sectors.                \par      South African shares barely closed in the black on\par  Wednesday as investors awaited the outcome of the latest\par  round of negotiations to end the country's longest-running\par  platinum sector strike.               \par  \par  NIGERIA MARKETS\par  Nigeria's naira          eased against the U.S. dollar on\par  Wednesday as banks bought the greenback on the interbank\par  market due to inadequate supply from offshore investors\par  participating at a bond auction, dealers said.\par                 \par  \par  NIGERIA SECURITY\par  Suspected Islamist militants have killed dozens of civilians\par  in three villages in northeastern Nigeria, a region now hit\par  by almost daily attacks, a security source and a victim's\par  relative said on Wednesday.               \par  \par  LAFARGE NIGERIA\par  The Nigerian unit of French cement marker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lafarge\f28 \uc2 \f2           \par  plans to seek shareholders' approval in July to raise 100\par  billion naira in public offer of debt or equity, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lafarge\par  Wapco\f28 \uc2 \f2             said on Wednesday.                    \par  \par  KENYA MARKETS\par  Kenya's shilling        strengthened modestly on Wednesday,\par  boosted by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par  while shares inched down.                \par  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 KENYA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  LENDING RATES\par  Kenya will introduce a new formula for banks to use in\par  pricing loans, seeking to bring down high interest rates that\par  have stifled lending to businesses and home buyers, the\par  Finance Ministry said on Wednesday.               \par  \par  EAST AFRICA PIPELINE    \par  Kenya, Uganda and South Sudan are expected to invite bids\par  this month for a single consultant to oversee the building of\par  an oil pipeline to transport crude to the Kenyan coast, a\par  senior Kenyan energy official said on Wednesday.\par                 \par  \par  UGANDA REFINERY\par  Companies from China, Japan, South Korea and Russia have\par  submitted bids to finance, build and operate Uganda's first\par  oil refinery, the energy ministry said on\par  Wednesday.               \par  \par  UGANDA LENDING RATE\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Uganda's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut its key lending rate             \par  by 50 basis points on Wednesday and hinted at further rate\par  cuts to safeguard growth in Uganda's economy.                \par  \par  BURUNDI TRADE\par  Burundi's trade deficit narrowed sharply to $159.4 million in\par  the first quarter of 2014 from $192.9 million in the same\par  period last year due to an appreciation of the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par  against the U.S. dollar, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on\par  Wednesday.               \par  \par  WEST AFRICA CRUDE OIL EXPORTS\par  Exports of West African crude oil to Asia are set to rise to\par  1.93 million barrels per day (bpd) in June from 1.72 million\par  bpd in May, a Reuters survey of traders showed on\par  Wednesday.               \par  \par  CAMEROON CHAD RAILWAY\par  Cameroon and Chad have reached an initial agreement to link\par  northeastern Cameroon to the neighbouring capital N'Djamena\par  by rail, according to officials from the two countries.\par                 \par  \par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 GENERAL ELECTRIC ANGOLA\f28 \uc2 \f2 General Electric\f28 \uc2 \f2         (\f28 \uc2 \f2 GE\f28 \uc2 \f2 ) will supply railway and energy\par  equipment to Angola in a $1 billion deal financed by the\par  U.S.-run Export-Import Bank (Ex-Im), officials and state-run\par  media said on Wednesday.               \par  \par  WEST AFRICAN BANK LENDING RATE\par  The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the eight nation West African franc zone\par  (BCEAO) kept its prime lending rate unchanged at 2.50 percent\par  on Wednesday and lowered its growth forecast for\par  2014.               \par  \par      For the latest precious metals report click on        \par      For the latest base metals report click on         \par      For the latest crude oil report click on\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-6-5T06:00:52.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140605ea650033s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
