\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Kenya \highlight\uc2 's shilling steady on prospect of  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 364 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Mai 2014\par 10:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par NAIROBI, May 29 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Kenya\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's shilling hovered below\par the 88 per dollar level on Thursday with market participants\par reluctant to break the psychologically important barrier after\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  signalled its intent to defend the local\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , traders said.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Kenya\f28 \uc2 \f2  sold dollars on Friday after the\par shilling fell through 88 and on Monday said it had ample foreign\par reserves to shore up a shilling that had weakened steadily\par during the first three weeks of May.\par     The bank's aggressive stance has for now halted the\par shilling's decline, due in part to market nerves following a\par series of bombings in the capital and the east African economy's\par main port city.\par     Leading commercial banks quoted the shilling at 87.80/90 on\par Thursday morning.\par     "Market players are very aware of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par So I think players will be a bit cautious," said Andlip Nazir,\par senior trader at \f28 \uc2 \f2 I&M Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par     "The shilling has been very quiet yesterday and today. We\par are expecting a very tight range of 87.80 and 87.90 bid and\par offer," Nazir said, adding the shilling might even firm slightly\par as end-month dollar demand from corporate clients tapers off. \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's governor, Njuguna Ndung'u, said on Monday\par that proceeds from a planned debut Eurobond issuance before the\par close of the fiscal year on June 30 would raise \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par reserves higher help the shilling appreciate.\par     "We expect the Eurobond flows expected from next month to\par give the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  a break from frequent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank\par of Africa\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in its daily market report.\par                ...........................Shilling spot rates\par                   .....................Shilling forward rates\par                            .......................Cross rates\par          ..................................Local contributors\par            \f28 \uc2 \f2 .......................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Kenya\f28 \uc2 \f2  Index\par           .....................Kenyan Bonds contributor pages\par                           \f28 \uc2 \f2 ...............Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  bill yields\par         ..................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par         .........................Horizontal repo transactions\par          ,       ................Daily interbank lending rate\par               .............................Kenya Bond pricing\par              ..................Real time Africa economic data\par  <ECI & AFR> ...........................African economic news\par           .................................NSE-20 Share Index\par          .................................NSE All Share Index\par              ...........................FT NSE Kenya 15 Index\par              .......................... FT NSE Kenya 25 Index\par   SPEED GUIDES:\par                      