\par\par \b \uc2 African Markets - Factors to watch on May 26\b0\par\par\uc2 658 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Mai 2014\par 07:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The following company announcements, scheduled economic indicators, debt and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market\par moves and political events may affect African markets on Monday.\par     - - - - -\par  GLOBAL MARKETS\par  Asian shares hit one-year high on Monday thanks to a strong\par  session on Wall Street and a decisive win for billionaire\par  Petro Poroshenko in Ukraine's presidential election.\par             \par  \par  WORLD OIL PRICES\par  Brent crude edged down towards $110 a barrel on Monday,\par  dipping further from last week's two-and-a-half month high\par  as worries over Ukraine eased slightly after its\par  presidential election.       \par  \par  SOUTH AFRICA CABINET\par  South African President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jacob Zuma\f28 \uc2 \f2  promoted deputy finance\par  minister Nhlanhla Nene to finance minister on Sunday,\par  replacing the widely respected Pravin Gordhan in a new\par  cabinet line-up to start a second five-year term in office.\par                 \par  \par  AFRICA ECONOMY\par  African economies are securing new funds through resource\par  finds or dollar bonds but many governments face questions\par  over how they use the money and risk being punished by\par  international capital markets.                 \par  \par  AFRICA DEBT\par  Yields on Kenyan Treasurybills are expected to edge slightly\par  higher in an auction likely to be under-subscribed next\par  week. The opposite should however be true for Nigeria, where\par  excess liquidity should drive demand for local debt, pushing\par  yields down.                \par  \par  EMERGING MARKETS\par  For the top emerging markets news, double click on\par             \par  \par  AFRICA STOCKS\par  For the latest news on African stocks, click on     \par  \par  SOUTH AFRICA MARKETS  \par  * South African stocks hit a record high for the second\par  straight day on Friday, but gains were limited as investors\par  cashed in recent advancers such as \f28 \uc2 \f2 SABMiller\f28 \uc2 \f2  SABJ.J and\par  Tiger Brands TBSJ.J.                \par  *  South Africa's rand touched a 1-1/2 week high against the\par  dollar on Friday, supported by a risk-positive global\par  environment, but could retreat next week if GDP data comes\par  in weaker than expected, undermining the case for more rate\par  hikes this year.                          \par  \par  NIGERIA MARKETS\par  *  Nigeria's budget deficit is now 1 percent of GDP\par  following a rebasing of its gross domestic product, from 1.9\par  percent before, finance minister Ngozi Okonjo-Iweala said in\par  a statement, after President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goodluck Jonathan\f28 \uc2 \f2  signed the\par  budget for 2014 into law.                \par  * Nigerian interbank lending rates fell to an average of\par  10.25 percent this week, compared with 12.41 percent last\par  week, as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kept its benchmark rate unchanged\par  but paid off matured treasury bills, boosting liquidity.\par                 \par  \par  NIGERIA INSECURITY\par  Suspected Islamist Boko Haram gunmen rampaged through three\par  villages in northern Nigeria, killing 28 people and burning\par  houses to the ground in a pattern of violence that has\par  become almost a daily occurrence, according to police and\par  witnesses.                \par  \par  KENYA MARKETS\par  The Kenyan shilling traded at 2-1/2 year lows on Friday amid\par  demand from importers for dollars and investor concerns over\par  a spate of bombings in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Kenya\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , with traders expecting the\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to fall further barring \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par  bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .                \par  \par  MALAWI ELECTION\par  Malawi's High Court on Saturday issued an injunction\par  stopping President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Joyce Banda\f28 \uc2 \f2  from interfering in the\par  electoral process, making her earlier decision to annul\par  national elections invalid and raising the risk of\par  post-election violence in the southern African country.\par                  \par  \par  DJIBOUTI ATTACK\par  At least two people were killed by double grenade blasts at\par  a busy restaurant popular with Westerners in Djibouti,\par  police said on Saturday.                \par  \par  GABON ECONOMY\par  Gabon wants to lure investors into its mining, manufacturing\par  and tourism sectors as it tries to reduce its dependence on\par  oil exports and court capital from countries other than\par  former colonial master France.                 \par  \par  SOUTH SUDAN OIL\par  Sudan has offered to supply materials, engineers and\par  electricity to South Sudan to speed up the repair of\par  oilfields damaged during a five month rebellion that has cut\par  output by a third, South Sudan's oil minister said on\par  Saturday.                     \par  \par  \par      For the latest precious metals report click on        \par      For the latest base metals report click on         \par      For the latest crude oil report click on\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-5-26T06:19:48.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140526ea5q00566\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
