\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Kenya shilling remains on back foot, stocks up\b0\par\par\uc2 749 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Mai 2014\par 16:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Shilling hits new 2-1/2 year low\par \par \uc2 * Stocks close higher, banking shares help (Adds markets close, stocks, bonds)\par \par \uc2 By George Obulutsa\par \par \uc2 NAIROBI, May 23 (Reuters) - The Kenyan shilling traded at 2-1/2 year lows on Friday amid demand from importers for dollars and investor concerns over a spate of bombings in \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with traders expecting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fall further barring \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On the Nairobi Securities Exchange, the main share index closed 0.2 percent higher, driven by bank stocks.\par \par \uc2 At close of trade at 1300 GMT, commercial banks quoted the shilling at 87.75/85 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the session the shilling passed through 88 to the dollar, a key technical dollar resistance level, hurt by a spate of bombings in the capital Nairobi and along the coast. Tourists have left in droves after travel warnings by Britain and the United States.\par \par \uc2 So far the shilling has retreated 1.65 percent against the dollar since January.\par \par \uc2 "There is strong demand from importers and manufacturers, while the inflows are scanty," said Andlip Nazir, senior trader at \uc2 I&M Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "After breaching the 88 level, 88.50 is a reasonable target if demand persists and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stay out."\par \par \uc2 The shilling has been aided by persistent liquidity mop ups by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Kenya\uc2 . By draining excess liquidity the bank makes it more expensive for banks to hold onto long dollar positions.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  mopped up on Friday 7.25 billion shillings, after seeking to mop up 12 billion shillings ($136.5 million) in excess liquidity.\par \par \uc2 "If CBK continues \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  (via repos), I think it will be kept in check below 88.00. It depends on determination of the CBK," said Julius Kiriinya, a trader at \uc2 African Banking Corporation\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, some traders said the mop-ups would not prevent a further decline in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have to sell a huge amount of dollars to stem the slide.\par \par \uc2 Kenya's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said this week the shilling's weakening was "temporary" due to the start of the dividend payment season, with Kenyan companies buying dollars to pay dividends to foreign investors, and not security-related concerns.\par \par \uc2 A grenade attack on a police vehicle in Kenya's port city of Mombasa on Thursday evening was just the latest incident in a string of attacks largely blamed on the Islamist group \uc2 al Shabaab\uc2 , based in neighbouring Somalia.\par \par \uc2 Al Shabaab\uc2 , which has fought a bloody seven year campaign to impose its interpretation of Islamic law inside Somalia, has said it wants to take revenge for Kenya's deployment of troops in the Horn of Africa nation.\par \par \uc2 Technical analysis of the shilling's 14-day and 50-day weighted moving averages also show that the shilling is expected to maintain a weakening trend in the near term.\par \par \uc2 On the Nairobi Securities Exchange, the main NSE-20 Share Index was up 10.52 points, or 0.2 percent, to close at 4,925.58 points.\par \par \uc2 Among the risers were shares in \uc2 Equity Bank\uc2  and \uc2 Kenya Commercial Bank\uc2 , which analysts said were still helped higher by their first quarter earnings performance.\par \par \uc2 Equity posted a 21 percent rise in first quarter pretax profit to 5.4 billion shillings, while KCB registered a 31 percent rise in first quarter pretax profit to 5.6 billion shillings.\par \par \uc2 Equity closed 2.6 percent higher at 39.75 shillings a share, while KCB ended the session up 0.5 percent at 46.75 shillings a share.\par \par \uc2 "For KCB and Equity, I would say it's mainly speculation. Banks are releasing their Q1 results, so you can also tie down the performance to that," Agnes Achieng, research analyst at Sterling Investment Bank, said.\par \par \uc2 On the secondary market, government bonds valued at 294.5 million shillings ($3.35 million) were traded, compared with 652 million shillings on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 ...........................Shilling spot rates\par \par \uc2 .....................Shilling forward rates\par \par \uc2 .......................Cross rates\par \par \uc2 ..................................Local contributors\par \par \uc2 .......................\b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Kenya\uc2  Index\par \par \uc2 .....................Kenyan Bonds contributor pages\par \par \uc2 ...............Treasury bill yields\par \par \uc2 ..................\b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 .........................Horizontal repo transactions\par \par \uc2 ,................Daily interbank lending rate\par \par \uc2 .............................Kenya Bond pricing\par \par \uc2 ..................Real time Africa economic data\par \par \uc2 <ECI & AFR> ...........................African economic news\par \par \uc2 .................................NSE-20 Share Index\par \par \uc2 .................................NSE All Share Index\par \par \uc2 ...........................FT NSE Kenya 15 Index\par \par \uc2 .......................... FT NSE Kenya 25 Index\par \par \uc2 SPEED 