\par\par \b \uc2 Kenyan shilling flat before expected pick-up in dollar demand\b0\par\par\uc2 324 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 2014\par 10:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par NAIROBI, May 16 (Reuters) - The Kenyan shilling was\par flat on Friday, with a key support level in traders' sights\par ahead of an expected pick-up next week in end-month demand for\par dollars.\par     At 0720 GMT, commercial banks posted the shilling at\par 87.40/50, unchanged from the previous day's close.\par     "The shilling will be under more pressure next week as we\par start the traditional end-of-the-month demand (for dollars),"\par said Robert Gatobu, a dealer at Bank of Africa.\par     The shilling might weaken past its 87.50 support level.\par "From next week we might try and break it. On the supply side\par there are minimal flows compared to the demand that is there,"\par Gatobu said.\par     Tourist arrivals, a key source of hard \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , have been\par cut by frequent gun and grenade attacks after \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Kenya intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par in neighbouring Somalia.\par     Visitors left coastal resorts on Thursday after Britain and\par the United States issued warnings against travel to parts of\par Kenya due to threats of attacks. \par     The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could eventually benefit from a\par government deal to settle a row over paying past contracts,\par which clears the way for a debut Eurobond worth up to $2\par billion. \par     "That paves way for the success of the Eurobond so maybe in\par two, three months from now, we will start seeing inflows coming\par in, which might protect the shilling from further weakening,"\par Gatobu said.\par                ...........................Shilling spot rates \par                   .............