\par\par \b \uc2 Kenyan shilling steady, eyes on liquidity mop-ups\b0\par\par\uc2 295 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 April 2014\par 10:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par NAIROBI, April 2 (Reuters) - The Kenyan shilling held\par steady against the dollar on Wednesday, with traders expecting\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to mop up liquidity to offer support to the\par shilling in the coming days.\par     At 0646 GMT, commercial banks quoted the shilling at\par 86.40/60 to the dollar, compared with Tuesday's close of\par 86.40/50.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Kenya\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (CBK) has been regularly\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the money markets to drain excess shilling\par liquidity in recent weeks, a trend which traders say should\par boost the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "We have not seen much (market) activity. Though with CBK\par mopping up aggressively, the expected trend is for a\par strengthening Kenya shilling," Sheikh Mehran, senior trader at\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kenya Commercial Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 , said.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Tuesday mopped up 1.55 billion shillings\par from the money markets using repurchase agreements at a weighted\par average rate of 8.297 percent. \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  frequently mopped up liquidity in March\par after overnight borrowing rates tumbled, making it a bit cheaper\par for banks to fund long dollar positions, which in turn put\par pressure on the shilling.\par     Traders said they forecast the shilling to trade in the\par 86.30 to 86.70 range in coming days.\par     \par       