\par\par \b \uc2 African Markets - Factors to watch on May 31\b0\par\par\uc2 757 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Mai 2013\par 07:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 The following company announcements, scheduled economic indicators, debt and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market moves and political events may affect African markets on Friday. - - - - - EVENTS: KENYA - \uc2 Kenya National Bureau of Statistics\uc2  to release May inflation data. The year-on-year inflation rate inched down to 4.11 percent in March from 4.45 percent a month earlier. UGANDA - The \uc2 Uganda Bureau of Statistics\uc2  to release May inflation data. The year-on-year inflation rate fell to 3.4 percent in the year to April from 4.0 percent a month earlier. ZAMBIA - \uc2 Zambia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to set bencmahr rate for May. In April, the bank left it main lending rate steady at 9.25 percent, saying inflation was likely to moderate in May because of an improved maize harvest. MAURITIUS - \uc2 Bank of Mauritius\uc2  auctions 273-day Treasury bills worth a total 600 million rupees ($19.20 million). GLOBAL MARKETS Asian shares recovered but the dollar stayed pressured on Friday after lacklustre U.S.\par \par \uc2  data eased concerns about an early end to the Federal Reserve's strong stimulus programme which has sharpened investor appetite for risk. WORLD OIL PRICES Brent futures held above $102 a barrel on Friday as the dollar softened on hopes the U.S. Federal Reserve would maintain its stimulus measures, offsetting demand worries stemming from an unexpected rise in crude stockpiles in the top oil consumer. EMERGING MARKETS For the top emerging markets news, double click on AFRICA STOCKS For the latest news on African stocks, click on AFRICA \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  U.S. President Barack Obama's trip to Tanzania at the end of June could provide a psychological boost to the shilling in the weeks ahead, while a bond sale in Ghana on Thursday is expected to bring only temporary relief to the faltering cedi. SOUTH AFRICA ECONOMY The South African economy is bogged down in old politics. Real GDP didn't even manage a 1 percent growth rate in the first quarter of 2013. SOUTH AFRICAN MARKETS South African stocks surged on Thursday as a weak rand lifted some of Johannesburg's worst performing shares this\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  year such as bullion  producers Harmony Gold          and\par  Gold Fields         .     \par     The rand breached 10 to the dollar for the first time in\par  more than four years on Thursday after an attempt by the\par  country's president to allay concerns over labour unrest\par  misfired badly.       \par  \par  KENYA MARKETS\par  * The Kenyan shilling        dipped on Thursday in late\par  demand for dollars by importers after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to sell dollars in the previous session, stayed\par  out.                \par  * Renewed economic activity following a smooth presidential\par  vote is driving demand for imports in Kenya, weakening the\par  shilling  and prompting wariness about the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par  response, including more \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .                \par  * The weighted average yield on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Kenya\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's 91-day Treasury bill\par             fell to 7.569 percent at an oversubscribed sale on\par  Thursday from 8.482 percent last week, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said.\par                 \par  \par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 BARCLAYS KENYA\f28 \uc2 \f2  Q1\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays Bank of Kenya\f28 \uc2 \f2           reported a 6 percent rise in