\par\par \b \uc2 AFRICA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  WEEKAHEAD-Election challenge hangs over Kenyan shilling\b0\par\par\uc2 800 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2013\par 14:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 NAIROBI, March 21 (Reuters) - Kenya's shilling is seen under pressure from market concerns about a legal challenge to this month's presidential election and routine end-month dollar demand, while \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are seen keeping Nigeria's naira rangebound.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 KENYA\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The Kenyan shilling will remain under pressure from end-month importer dollar demand and concern over a legal challenge to this month's presidential election.\par \par \uc2 The shilling has been rangebound between 85.00-86.00 since defeated candidate Raila Odinga, the country's prime minister, challenged the result of a broadly peaceful March 4 vote.\par \par \uc2 At 1120 GMT, commercial banks quoted the shilling at 85.70/80 per dollar, weaker than last Thursday's 85.30/50 close.\par \par \uc2 "There might be a little bit of demand from importers but the shilling might not cross 86," said Jeremiah Kendagor, head of trading at \uc2 Kenya Commercial Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The market is in limbo with both sides evenly matched as players wait for the election petition to be resolved."\par \par \uc2 The possibility of a re-run of the election if the court rules in favour of Odinga has unnerved some.\par \par \uc2 UGANDA\par \par \uc2 The Ugandan shilling is seen on the back foot against the dollar this week due to end-month demand for hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from manufacturers and fuel importers.\par \par \uc2 Commercial banks quoted the shilling 2,625/2,635, stronger than last Thursday's close of 2,640/2,650.\par \par \uc2 "We're likely to get some demand from manufacturers since we're moving close to the end of the month so I see scope for some depreciation of the shilling," said Shahzad Kamaluddin, trader at Crane Bank.\par \par \uc2 The shilling, which is up 2.3 percent versus the dollar this year is supported in the short term by high borrowing costs.\par \par \uc2 "I doubt the unit will break the 2,670 level on the upper side," said a trader at a leading commercial bank.\par \par \uc2 TANZANIA\par \par \uc2 The Tanzanian shilling might firm slightly against the dollar in the days ahead as companies convert greenbacks into the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to pay taxes.\par \par \uc2 Traders quoted the shilling at 1,617/1,627 to the dollar on Thursday, stronger than the 1,625/1,630 level of last week.\par \par \uc2 "The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely stay at the same levels or could appreciate slightly against the dollar in the days ahead because customers are changing dollars into shillings to settle tax obligation as we approach the quarter end," said Fred Siwali, a dealer at CRDB Bank.\par \par \uc2 "(The shilling) has been helped by the fact that we don't see a lot of demand for dollars in the market at the moment."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Tanzania\uc2  traded $38.92 million on the interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market over the past week.\par \par \uc2 NIGERIA\par \par \uc2 The naira is seen rangebound against the dollar, said traders who expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and tame any volatility due to anticipated dollar sales by oil companies.\par \par \uc2 The naira traded at 158.95 to the dollar on the interbank market on Thursday at 1033 GMT, weaker than the 158.80 it closed at the previous day.\par \par \uc2 "The market opened lower this morning because of strong dollar demand, but fear of a likely \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept the market in check," one dealer said.\par \par \uc2 Waning offshore interest in local debt has dampened the flow of dollars into the market, weighing on the naira.\par \par \uc2 GHANA\par \par \uc2 Ghana's cedi will stay under pressure next week on unmet dollar-craving by local firms for their imports and seasonal repatriation of funds by multinationals, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 The local unit slumped to a seven-month low on Wednesday at 1.9400 against the dollar, mainly on end-of-quarter corporate demand for the greenback amid weak supply.\par \par \uc2 Market players said the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could slide further to touch the 1.9500 levels.\par \par \uc2 "Multinational companies are remitting funds outside the country to their parent companies," said Ama Ofowaah Boateng of the Accra-based Databank Financial Research group\par \par \uc2 Stanbic Ghana trader Christopher Nettey said: "There has been no \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  support recently - We may reach the 1.9500 psychological resistant level next week unless we see some action from them," Nettey added.\par \par \uc2 ZAMBIA\par \par \uc2 Economic woes in the euro zone may dampen appetite for emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as investors run to the dollar, keeping Zambia's kwacha under pressure, traders said.\par \par \uc2 Commercial banks quoted the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Africa's top copper producer at 5.380 per dollar, matching last week.\par \par \uc2 Big falls beyond 5.400 were likely to be challenged by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , one trader said.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Kevin Mwanza, Chris Mfula, Kwasi Kpodo, Oludare Mayowa, Elias Biryabarema and Fumbuka Ng'wanakilala; editing by Ron Askew)\par \par \uc2 AFRICA-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 / | ABN | M | D | AFN | RBN | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130321e93l000ry\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
