\par\par \b \uc2 African Markets - Factors to watch on Feb 8\b0\par\par\uc2 617 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Februar 2013\par 07:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 NAIROBI, Feb 8 (Reuters) - The following company announcements, scheduled economic indicators, debt and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market moves and political events may affect African markets on Friday.\par \par \uc2 - - - - -\par \par \uc2 GLOBAL MARKETS\par \par \uc2 Asian shares edged up on Friday after China's trade data for January\par \par \uc2 handily beat forecasts to underscore a recovery trend, but prices were\par \par \uc2 capped by investors seeking to book profits before next week's Chinese new\par \par \uc2 year holidays.\par \par \uc2 WORLD OIL PRICES\par \par \uc2 Brent futures rose towards $118 per barrel on Friday, heading for a fourth\par \par \uc2 weekly gain as robust trade data from China bolstered the outlook for\par \par \uc2 demand, while escalating tensions in the Middle East stoked concerns over\par \par \uc2 supply.\par \par \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS\par \par \uc2 For the top emerging markets news, double click on\par \par \uc2 AFRICA STOCKS\par \par \uc2 For the latest news on African stocks, click on\par \par \uc2 AFRICA NEWS\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For the latest news on Africa, click on                 \par AFRICA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     \par The Tanzanian shilling is expected to continue its recovery from a 14-month\par low due to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , while \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Kenya\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and Uganda's shillings\par are seen stabilising.                \par SOUTH AFRICA MARKETS\par * South African stocks gained on Thursday, pushing major indices back\par towards a record high set earlier this week as battered retailers extended\par a recovery to a third straight day.     \par * The rand firmed on the dollar in afternoon trade but was struggling to\par make significant gains after soft manufacturing data hit prospects for\par economic growth in South Africa.       \par NIGERIA OIL\par * \f28 \uc2 \f2 Exxon Mobil\f28 \uc2 \f2          on Thursday declared force majeure on Nigeria's\par benchmark Qua Iboe crude oil exports due to pipeline repair work, the\par company's local unit said, cutting output from Africa's top producer. \par              \par * \f28 \uc2 \f2 Royal Dutch Shell Plc\f28 \uc2 \f2 's          local Nigerian unit has declared force\par majeure on gas supplies to the country's 22 million tonne-a-year liquefied\par natural gas (NLNG) export terminal, the company said on Thursday. \par              \par NIGERIA POLITICS    \par Nigeria's four main opposition movements announced a merger, posing the\par sternest threat in years to President Goodluck Jonathan's ruling party\par ahead of elections in 2015.                \par ANGOLA DIAMOND\par Angola's Catoca, one of the world's largest diamond producers, could invest\par in diamond exploration and production in nearby Zimbabwe, Angola's mines\par minister said on Thursday.                  \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 KENYA MARKETS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Kenya's benchmark share index jumped nearly 1 percent to strike a\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 25-month high on Thursday, extending gains to a seventh session and buoyed\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 by expectation of a strong earnings session that begins next week.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * The weighted average yield on Kenya's benchmark 91-day Treasury bills\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par          rose to 8.229 percent at auction on Thursday from 8.164 percent\par last week, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said.                \par GHANA STOCKS\par Shares in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Guinness Ghana Breweries Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2            climbs 1 percent after\par the beverage maker reported a 115 percent jump in net profit for the\par six-months to December 2012, traders said.                \par TANZANIA C/A DEFICIT    \par Tanzania's current account deficit narrowed 14 percent to $3.44 billion in\par 2012 helped by a strong jump in export revenues even though gold export\par volumes dipped, its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on Thursday.                   \par MAURITIUS INFLATION\par Mauritius' annual average inflation rate              fell to 3.7 percent\par in January from 3.9 percent in December, the statistics office said on\par Friday.                  \par SOUTH SUDAN FARMING    \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Khartoum\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Sudan's oldest bank, wants to boost its agricultural\par finance business with the help of Gulf Arab banks after winning the African\par country's first-ever international rating, its head said on Thursday. \par              \par \par   For the latest precious metals report click on        \par   For the latest base metals report click on         \par   For the latest crude oil report click on       \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ($1 = 87.6250 Kenyan shillings)\f28 \par \par \uc2 AFRICA-FACTORS/ | ABN | M | D | AFN | E | RBN | UKI | AUF | U | FSC | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130208e928000ce\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
