\par\par \b \uc2 AFRICA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  WEEKAHEAD-Tanzania shilling recovery set to continue\b0\par\par\uc2 773 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Februar 2013\par 15:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  JOHANNESBURG, Feb 7 (Reuters) - The Tanzanian shilling is expected to continue its recovery from a 14-month low due to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Uganda's shillings are seen stabilising.    \par \par \uc2  TANZANIA\par \par \uc2  Tanzania's shilling is seen extending gains made this week against the dollar after the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a 14-month low at the beginning of the month.\par \par \uc2  Market players said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been injecting dollars into the system to satisfy demand and had also temporarily barred some banks it suspected of speculative trading from making transactions.\par \par \uc2  The shilling fell more than 3 percent against the dollar between Jan. 1 and Feb. 1 when it hit a bid price of 1,624, a level last seen on Dec. 12, 2011. \par \par \uc2  Market players quoted the shilling at 1,610/1,620 to the dollar on Thursday, stronger than 1,620/1,630 a week ago.\par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to try to halt the shilling from further depreciation. This has included issuing temporary trading bans for a maximum of three days to some commercial banks that were deemed to be taking part in speculation trading," said a trader at a commercial bank in Dar es Salaam.\par \par \uc2  UGANDA\par \par \uc2  Uganda's shilling is seen rangebound next week with a bias to weaken on expectations of higher dollar demand from fuel importers ahead of March elections in neighbouring Kenya.\par \par \uc2  At 1015 GMT commercial banks in Kampala quoted the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of east Africa's third-largest economy at 2,650/2,660, unchanged from last Thursday's close.\par \par \uc2  "Dollar demand from energy and manufacturing firms has been largely dead since the beginning of the year but now Kenyan elections are only weeks away and sooner rather than later this demand will come in," said Benon Okwenje, a trader at \uc2 Stanbic Bank\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2  "Once that demand starts coming in the shilling should start to see upward pressure again."\par \par \uc2  Landlocked Uganda is heavily dependent on Kenya's Mombasa port to bring in goods. \par \par \uc2  The March presidential vote is the first since a disputed election in 2007 which unleashed nationwide violence that sent Kenya's economy, the region's biggest, into a tailspin. The unrest also blocked major trading routes, sending the price of imported goods skywards in Uganda, Rwanda and southern Sudan.\par \par \uc2  Violence cannot be ruled out in this year's vote and importers are wary, Okwneje said.\par \par \uc2  KENYA\par \par \uc2  Kenya's shilling is seen holding steady against the dollar next week, supported by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's actions to tighten liquidity to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid fears of unrest around next month's general election.\par \par \uc2  The shilling has held steady at 87.50/70 in three straight trading sessions this week and is barely changed from last Thursday's close of 87.45/65.\par \par \uc2  "The interbank interest rates are up and liquidity has tightened since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has continued to soak up supplies," said Ignatius Chicha, head of markets at Citibank.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been draining shillings from the market daily and sold dollars in seven separate sessions this year to bolster the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . This has driven the interbank lending rate higher. \par \par \uc2  The shilling is down 1.6 percent against the dollar so far this year, pressured lower by banks holding long dollar positions and importers stockpiling hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid fears of violence linked to general elections next month.\par \par \uc2  NIGERIA\par \par \uc2  The naira strengthened against the dollar on Thursday after state-energy firm NNPC offered about $450 million to some lenders, but dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  should edge lower next week on the strength of greenback demand by fuel importers.\par \par \uc2  The local unit was trading around 157.20 to the dollar at 1031 GMT, stronger than its 157.40 close the previous day.\par \par \uc2  "The naira appreciated this morning as the news of NNPC dollar sales hit the market, but the gain may not last longer than this week because of strong demand for the dollar by importers," one trader said.\par \par \uc2  ZAMBIA\par \par \uc2  The kwacha is likely to firm next week due to increased supply of dollars from local and offshore players.\par \par \uc2  The kwacha gained 1.5 percent over the week and was trading at 5.310 at 1120 GMT on Thursday from 5.390 a week ago.\par \par \uc2  "We have seen substantial dollar supply from offshore players and locals and that have given support to the kwacha," one commercial bank trader said. \par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Kevin Mwanza, Fumbuka Ng'wanakilala, Elias Biryabarema, Oludare Mayowa and Chris Mfula; Editing by Tosin Sulaiman)\par \par \uc2 AFRICA-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  | AFN | ABN | D | M | SF | DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130207e9270017v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
