\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Kenya shilling recovers on cbank support, shares steady\b0\par\par\uc2 529 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 2013\par 16:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Cbank injects dollars for the 7th session this year\par \par \uc2 * Oil sector dollar orders weigh on shilling\par \par \uc2 * Investors await firms full-year earnings\par \par \uc2 (Adds markets close, stocks)\par \par \uc2 By Kevin Mwanza\par \par \uc2 NAIROBI, Jan 29 (Reuters) - The Kenyan shilling recouped earlier losses to finish Tuesday's session flat, helped by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  injecting an undisclosed amount of dollars into the market, while shares were barely changed.\par \par \uc2 The shilling slipped 0.4 percent within 30 minutes of Tuesday's session starting, touching 87.80/88.00 per dollar, a level it was last at on Jan. 5, 2012.\par \par \uc2 However, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  recovered to close the session at 87.50/75, the same level it finished at on Monday, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Kenya\uc2  sold dollars directly to commercial banks.\par \par \uc2 The bank has now pumped dollars into the market in seven different trading sessions this year to support the shilling, which is down 1.8 percent against the greenback in 2013.\par \par \uc2 Due to the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have dropped for four consecutive weeks to $5.177 billion last Friday, from $5.396 billion on Dec. 28.\par \par \uc2 "With the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , 88.00 is still the initial support level," said John Muli, a trader at African Banking Corporation.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also been mopping up liquidity using repurchase agreements (repo) since last year to support the shilling.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the bank received bids worth 8.7 billion shillings ($99.3 million) for the 15 billion shillings it had offered in repurchase agreements that day. It accepted all the bids at a weighted average interest rate of 6.7 percent.\par \par \uc2 Traders said liquidity had also tightened in the market due to government debt payments, with overnight interest rates on the interbank market rising steadily over 11 straight sessions to 6.67 percent on Monday.\par \par \uc2 At the Nairobi Securities Exchange, the benchmark NSE-20 Share Index fell 0.01 percent to 4,402.75 points, as the market waited for firms to post their full year results.\par \par \uc2 "Prices on most counters seem to have stabilised. Investors are positioning for company full-year earnings in February," said Faith Atiti, an analyst at NIC Securities.\par \par \uc2 Safaricom\uc2 , the country's leading telecoms operator and one of the most traded stocks on the bourse, fell 1.9 percent to 5.30 shillings a share. It accounted for more than half of Tuesday's traded volume.\par \par \uc2 In the fixed income market, government bonds worth 973 million shillings were traded, up from 602 million shillings traded on Monday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par             ...........................Shilling spot rates\par                .....................Shilling forward rates\par                         .......................Cross rates\par       ..................................Local contributors\par         \f28 \uc2 \f2 .......................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Kenya\f28 \uc2 \f2  Index\par        .....................Kenyan Bonds contributor pages\par                        ...............Treasury bill yields\par      ..................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  open ma