\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Importers weaken Kenyan shilling, banks lift stocks\b0\par\par\uc2 624 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 September 2012\par 09:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Shilling seen weakening on end-month dollar demand\par \par \uc2 * Cheaper cost of credit spurs interest in banking stocks\par \par \uc2 (Recasts market close, adds stocks)\par \par \uc2 By Beatrice Gachenge\par \par \uc2 NAIROBI, Sept 18 (Reuters) - Importer dollar demand pushed the Kenyan shilling lower against the dollar for the second straight day on Tuesday although greenback inflows from the tea sector helped offset some of the losses, and banks helped to drive stocks higher.\par \par \uc2 At the market close, commercial banks posted the shilling at 84.80/85.00 to the dollar, 0.3 percent weaker than Monday's close of 84.65/85.\par \par \uc2 "We have seen increased demand coming from the energy and oil sectors and that has pushed it higher (weaker)," said Dickson Magecha, a trader at \uc2 Standard Chartered\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We saw a bit of tea in the afternoon and that helped the shilling recoup some of its losses."\par \par \uc2 Kenya is the world's biggest exporter of black tea, and the crop is one of its largest \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  earners, raking in $1.27 billion in 2011.\par \par \uc2 Traders said there was room for the shilling to weaken further this week, under pressure from dollar-seeking importers looking to meet their end-month payment obligations.\par \par \uc2 "I would imagine if the market is volatile they (\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) would come and sell (dollars)."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2  (CBK) has regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market this year, frequently mopping up excess liquidity via repurchase agreements (repos) and occasionally selling dollars directly to commercial banks to try to take shillings out of the system.\par \par \uc2 "CBK's ... \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market are targeted at reducing volatility in the adjustment patch, and not to support a particular level or direction of the exchange rate," bank Governor Njuguna Ndung'u said in the bank's September newsletter.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  absorbed 8 billion shillings ($119 million) having received bids worth 5.05 billion shillings. It accepted all bids via the seven-day, 14-day, 21-day and 28-day tenures, between 7.8 percent and 8.488 percent.\par \par \uc2 On the Nairobi Securities Exchange, the main share index NSE 20-Share index broke a two-day losing streak, inching up 6.36 points to 3,956.54 points.\par \par \uc2 Equities analysts said healthy foreign appetite for banking stocks had lifted the market. The country's largest bank by assets, \uc2 Kenya Commercial Bank\uc2  closed up 1 percent to 27.25 shillings, while Co-operative Bank edged 1.2 percent higher to 12.40 shillings.\par \par \uc2 "The market anticipated a drop in lending rates, which could be a contributing factor," said Johnson Nderi, head of research at Suntra Investment. Lower lending rates were seen boosting banks' loan books, he said.\par \par \uc2 Most commercial banks have cut their interest rates after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Kenya\uc2  cut its key lending rate (CBR) by a record 350 basis point to 13 percent this month, easing the cost of funding.\par \par \uc2 Typically, cheap access to credit helps banks to enjoy enlarged loan books, pointing to strong performance of the sector.\par \par \uc2 In the debt markets, government bonds worth 4.76 billion shillings were traded, marginally down from Monday's close of 4.87 billion shillings. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par             ...........................Shilling spot rates\par                .....................Shilling forward rates\par                         .......................Cross rates\par       ..................................Local contributors\par         \f28 \uc2 \f2 .......................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Kenya\f28 \uc2 \f2  Index\par        .....................Kenyan Bonds contributor pages\par                        ...............Treasury bill yields\par      ..................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par      .........................Horizontal repo transactions\par       ,       ................Daily interbank lending rate\par            .............................Kenya Bond pricing\par           ..................Real time Africa economic data\par <ECI & AFR> ...........................African economic news\par        .................................NSE-20 Share Index\par       .................................NSE All Share Index\par           ...........................FT NSE Kenya 15 Index\par           .......................... FT NSE Kenya 25 Index\par  SPEED GUIDES:\par                                  \par          \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Beatrice Gachenge; Editing by Richard Lough)\f28 \par \par \uc2 KENYA-MARKETS/ (UPDATE 1) | ABN | M | E | RBN | AFN | D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120921e89i000g0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
