\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Kenyan shilling, shares hold steady\b0\par\par\uc2 479 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 2012\par 10:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Shilling seen supported by cbank \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2  Airways\uc2  weighs on main share index\par \par \uc2 (Adds markets close, stocks)\par \par \uc2 By Kevin Mwanza\par \par \uc2 NAIROBI, Aug 23 (Reuters) - The Kenyan shilling was steady against the dollar on Thursday, with the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  expected to be supported in coming days by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  liquidity mop-ups, while shares dipped marginally on a steep fall by \uc2 Kenya Airways\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At the 1300 GMT market close, commercial banks quoted the shilling at 83.90/84.10 per dollar, barely changed from Wednesday's close of 83.95/84.05.\par \par \uc2 "There seems to be some demand creeping at below 84.00, but with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  mopping up liquidity we expect the shilling to be steady at this level," said Duncan Kinuthia, head of trading at \uc2 Commercial Bank of Africa\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Traders said they also expected debt auctions to help absorb extra shillings from the market, on top of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's frequent use of repurchase agreements (repos) to drain liquidity.\par \par \uc2 The bank mopped up 2.65 billion shillings ($31.6 million) at a weighted average rate of 9.96 percent in seven-day repos on Thursday, after it received offers of 7.65 billion shillings for the 8 billion shillings it had offered.\par \par \uc2 At government debt auctions this week, yields on the two-year bond, six-month and three-month paper inched lower after demand hit 45 billion shillings, well above the 18 billion shillings the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had offered.\par \par \uc2 At the Nairobi Securities Exchange, the main NSE-20 share index shed 0.05 percent to 3,817.70 points, dragged down by \uc2 Kenya Airways\uc2 , which tumbled 5.6 percent to 12.80 shillings.\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 Kenya Airways\uc2  announced staff cuts but investors feel that's not enough to remedy its high \b \highlight22\uc2 operational\b0 \highlight\uc2  cost that is largely fuel expenses," said Rufus Mwanyasia, an analyst at Tsavo Securities.\par \par \uc2 In the debt market, the yield on the benchmark 91-day Treasury bills on sale on Thursday plunged 168 basis points to 8.583 percent, falling below the repo rate.\par \par \uc2 Mwanyasia said he expected subscription rates at coming sales to fall as commercial banks sought better returns in the money market.\par \par \uc2 At the bourse, government bond worth 6 billion shillings were traded, up from 3.5 billion shillings on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par             ...........................Shilling spot rates \par                .....................Shilling forward rates \par                         .......................Cross rates \par       ..................................Local contributors \par         \f28 \uc2 \f2 .......................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Kenya\f28 \uc2 \f2  Index \par        .....................Kenyan Bonds contributor pages \par                        ...............Treasury bill yields \par      ..................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par      .........................Horizontal repo transactions \par       ,       ................Daily interbank lending rate \par            .............................Kenya Bond pricing \par           ..................Real time Africa economic data \par <ECI & AFR> ..........................