\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Kenyan shilling extends tumble to 103 vs dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 366 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2011\par 08:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Heavy dollar buying as euro zone woes weigh\par \par \uc2 * Markets on alert for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 (Adds details, traders quotes)\par \par \uc2 By Beatrice Gachenge and Kevin Mwanza\par \par \uc2 NAIROBI, Sept 27 (Reuters) - The Kenyan shilling extended losses on Tuesday, falling to a fresh record low of 103\par \par \uc2 against the dollar, driven by heavy dollar buying against the backdrop of a worsening euro zone debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday marked the 29th time this year the shilling has plumbed a new low, traders said, and the market was looking to the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But the spate of all-time lows suggest investors and companies have little confidence in the bank's ability to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  even vaguely on an even keel, and when the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars on Monday it did little to bolster the shilling.\par \par \uc2 At 0702 GMT, commercial banks were quoting the shilling at 102.70/90, weaker than Monday's close of 102.00/20.\par \par \uc2 "We are in an all new territory right now and it's not clear where it could go from here. Guys are watching if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be back in today," said Wilson Mutai, a trader at African Banking Corporation.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold on Monday an unspecified amount of dollars for the fifth time this September in an attempt to support the shilling. Traders were worried the bank would inject more shillings as last week's 15.23 billion shilling ($149.2 million) reverse repo matures on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "It is more of panic buying. Some people are buying forward and those are the ones putting pressure on the shilling," said Duncan Kinuthia, head of trading at \uc2 Commercial Bank of Africa\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ...........................Shilling spot rates \par <0#KESF=>.....................Shilling forward rates \par .......................Cross rates \par ..................................Local contributors \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 .......................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Kenya\f28 \uc2 \f2  Index \par .....................Kenyan Bonds contributor pages \par ...............Treasury bill yields \par ..................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par .........................Horizontal repo transactions \par , ................Daily interbank lending rate \par <0#KETSYSTR=>.............................Kenya Bond pricing \par ..................Real time Africa economic data \par <ECI & AFR> ...........................African economic news \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SPEED GUIDES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ($1 = 102.100 Kenyan Shillings)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Editing by Yara Bayoumy; Editing by John Stonestreet)\f28 \par \par \uc2 KENYA-MARKETS/  (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110930e79r000by\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
