\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW-UPDATE 2-Kenya cenbank says committed to free  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  rate\b0\par\par\uc2 450 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2011\par 18:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Kenya central banker says \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures only temporary\par \par \uc2 * Says not trying to fight market trend\par \par \uc2 * Sees food price inflation falling by end-September\par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes and background)\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, Sept 27 (Reuters) - Kenya's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is committed to maintaining a freely traded exchange rate and sees current \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts as a temporary measure to fight market panic, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's governor said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Kenya\uc2  earlier on Tuesday said it planned to trade foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly with key economic sectors, remarks that helped lift the Kenyan shilling off a record low. For details see [ID:nL5E7KR0GN].\par \par \uc2 "When everybody panics, you have to come up with measures to try and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , not to control the direction of the market, but to stem panic. That is not moving away from a floating exchange rate per se," \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Njuguna Ndung'u told Reuters in a telephone interview from Cancun, in Mexico.\par \par \uc2 The Kenyan shilling <KES=>, which is the world's second-worst-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year according to Reuters data, has sunk more than 5 percent since last Friday after remarks from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spooked some observers who feared a retreat from free-market policies.\par \par \uc2 Kenya's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its benchmark rate this month after concerns grew that policymakers favored spurring growth over tackling a surge in inflation.\par \par \uc2 A steep slump in the county's shilling could worsen price pressures by inflaming import prices.\par \par \uc2 "We are not going to institute capital controls in Kenya," Ndung'u said, adding that the shilling had suffered losses due to the global sell-off in riskier assets, such as emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , on fears about Europe's debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 Inflation in Kenya has been fed in part by food shortages due to drought engulfing the Horn of Africa region, as well as high oil energy prices.\par \par \uc2 "The food problem is being solved gradually and by the end of this month food inflation will start coming down. We will wait to see how fuel oil prices are coming and, obviously, that will have an effect on the exchange rate," Ndung'u said.\par \par \uc2 He said any change in monetary policy would depend on developments in inflation and a widening gap in the balance of payments.\par \par \uc2 Kenya's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised rates this month by 75 basis points to fight rampant inflation, taking benchmark credit costs to 7 percent. Inflation is seen hitting 17.4 percent in September, according to a Reuters poll, from 16.67 percent in August.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Michael O'Boyle; Editing by Leslie Adler and James Dalgleish)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 KENYA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2, INTERVIEW)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110927e79r000xp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
