\par\par \b \uc2 African Markets - Factors to watch on Sept 14\b0\par\par\uc2 1,157 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2011\par 07:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 NAIROBI, Sept 14 (Reuters) - The following company announcements, scheduled economic indicators, debt and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market moves and political events may affect African markets on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 - - - - -\par \par \uc2 EVENTS:\par \par \uc2 KENYA - Kenya's Monetary Policy Committee holds\par \par \uc2 special meeting on situation in financial markets.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a chance to restore stability\par \par \uc2 to the country's money and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 markets and win back market confidence, if it\par \par \uc2 aggressively raises interest rates at an emergency\par \par \uc2 meeting on Sept. 14, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 KENYA-TBILLS - The government will this week\par \par \uc2 auction 182-day Treasury bills worth 6.5 billion\par \par \uc2 shillings ($69 million).\par \par \uc2 KENYA-FUEL - Watching out for the latest fuel\par \par \uc2 price review. The new prices take effect on Sept\par \par \uc2 15.\par \par \uc2 MAURITIUS - The \uc2 Bank of Mauritius\uc2  sells new\par \par \uc2 10-year bond \uc2 Bank of Mauritius\uc2  to sell 2 billion\par \par \uc2 Mauritius rupees ($70 million) of new 10-year\par \par \uc2 Treasury bonds maturing on Sept. 16, 2021. The\par \par \uc2 coupon rate will be set equal to or higher than\par \par \uc2 the lowest accepted yield of the auction\par \par \uc2 GLOBAL MARKETS\par \par \uc2 Asian stocks, U.S. index futures and the euro fell\par \par \uc2 on Wednesday as investors remained unconvinced\par \par \uc2 that euro zone leaders have a coherent plan to\par \par \uc2 tackle the bloc's sovereign debt problems, which\par \par \uc2 many fear could trigger a new banking crisis.\par \par \uc2 EURO ZONE CRISIS\par \par \uc2 International alarm over Europe's debt crisis hit\par \par \uc2 new heights on Tuesday, with U.S. President Barack\par \par \uc2 Obama pressing the bloc's big countries to show\par \par \uc2 leadership as talk of a Greek default escalated\par \par \uc2 and markets heaped pressure on Italy.\par \par \uc2 WORLD OIL PRICES\par \par \uc2 Oil fell on Wednesday, pulling U.S. crude off\par \par \uc2 six-week highs, as investors saw little upside\par \par \uc2 from declining inventories in an environment where\par \par \uc2 the euro zone debacle is taking precedence over\par \par \uc2 tightening supply.\par \par \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS\par \par \uc2 The BRICS major emerging economies are in\par \par \uc2 preliminary talks on increasing their holdings\par \par \uc2 of euro-denominated bonds to help ease Europe's\par \par \uc2 debt crisis, a senior Brazilian government\par \par \uc2 official told Reuters on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 For the top emerging markets news, double click on\par \par \uc2 AFRICA STOCKS\par \par \uc2 For the latest news on African stocks, click on\par \par \uc2 AFRICA FIXED INCOME\par \par \uc2 For news on African fixed income, click on\par \par \uc2 AFRICA BOND AUCTIONS\par \par \uc2 The following is a selection of domestic debt\par \par \uc2 auctions expected from frontier African\par \par \uc2 governments this week:\par \par \uc2 AFRICA DEBT\par \par \uc2 Ugandan yields are likely to climb significantly\par \par \uc2 at an auction of 3-year and 5-year bonds next\par \par \uc2 week, while Ghanaian yields are expected to remain\par \par \uc2 stable, reflecting the outlook for inflation.\par \par \uc2 AFRICA BANKING\par \par \uc2 South Africa's FirstRand is still looking\par \par \uc2 for opportunities in Nigeria, where bank\par \par \uc2 valuations are becoming "more realistic", its\par \par \uc2 chief executive said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 SOUTH AFRICA MARKETS\par \par \uc2 South Africa's rand gained against the dollar on\par \par \uc2 Tuesday, bouncing from 5-week lows as exporters\par \par \uc2 came in the market and sentiment towards risky\par \par \uc2 assets improved in late trade.\par \par \uc2 NIGERIA SECURITY\par \par \uc2 Eight suspected members of a Nigerian Islamist\par \par \uc2 sect appeared in court on Tuesday charged with\par \par \uc2 carrying out a series of bombings and shootings\par \par \uc2 between March and July this year that killed a\par \par \uc2 total of 25 people.\par \par \uc2 NIGERIA INFLATION\par \par \uc2 Nigeria's consumer price inflation is seen\par \par \uc2 steadying around 9.5 percent in August after\par \par \uc2 unexpectedly falling to a more than three-year low\par \par \uc2 of 9.4 percent in July, the median view of 10\par \par \uc2 economists polled by Reuters showed.\par \par \uc2 KENYA POLITICS\par \par \uc2 Kenya's cabinet on Tuesday proposed delaying next\par \par \uc2 year's elections by four months, a suggestion that\par \par \uc2 risked angering citizens determined politicians\par \par \uc2 should stick to a timetable set out in the\par \par \uc2 country's new constitution.\par \par \uc2 KENYA MARKETS\par \par \uc2 The Kenyan shilling gained ground against\par \par \uc2 the dollar on Tuesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold\par \par \uc2 dollars to commercial banks, its second such\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in two weeks, traders said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 KENYA\b0 \highlight\uc2  SECURITY\par \par \uc2 Gunmen who attacked a British tourist couple at a\par \par \uc2 luxury resort in Kenya were part of a larger gang\par \par \uc2 and took advantage of light security at the\par \par \uc2 Kenya-Somalia maritime border, an anti-terrorism\par \par \uc2 officer told Reuters on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 KENYA BOND\par \par \uc2 Kenya will auction next week a two year Treasury\par \par \uc2 bond worth 10 billion shillings\par \par \uc2 ($104.74 million) at an annual coupon rate of\par \par \uc2 10.50 pct, its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 TANZANIA GDP\par \par \uc2 Tanzania's economic growth slowed to 6.7 percent\par \par \uc2 in the second quarter of 2011 versus a 7.2 percent\par \par \uc2 expansion in the same period a year ago after\par \par \uc2 mining slowed sharply, but the transport and\par \par \uc2 communication sector mitigated the decline by\par \par \uc2 rising solidly, data showed on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 TANZANIA/UGANDA POWER\par \par \uc2 Tanzania and Uganda have signed an agreement to\par \par \uc2 build a 16 megawatt (MW) hydropower plant on a\par \par \uc2 river shared by the two east African countries.\par \par \uc2 UGANDA BONDS\par \par \uc2 Offshore demand for Ugandan debt is likely to hit\par \par \uc2 its strongest level since 2008 at a bond auction\par \par \uc2 on Wednesday, the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said, as\par \par \uc2 external investors chase after yields as high as\par \par \uc2 20 percent.\par \par \uc2 UGANDA OIL\par \par \uc2 London-based explorer \uc2 Tullow Oil\uc2 's\par \par \uc2 long-running deal to bring France's Total\par \par \uc2 and China's CNOOC into a $10\par \par \uc2 billion oil project in Uganda is near its\par \par \uc2 conclusion, the east African country's energy\par \par \uc2 minister said.\par \par \uc2 UGANDA SECURITY\par \par \uc2 Two suspects in Uganda pleaded guilty on Tuesday\par \par \uc2 to murder and terrorism charges connected to twin\par \par \uc2 bomb blasts that struck soccer fans in the east\par \par \uc2 African nation's capital last year and killed 79\par \par \uc2 people, a court official said.\par \par \uc2 ETHIOPIA INFLATION\par \par \uc2 Ethiopia's year-on-year inflation jumped to 40.6\par \par \uc2 percent in August from 39.2 percent a month before\par \par \uc2 as food prices rose, especially for cereals, the\par \par \uc2 statistics office said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 ZIMBABWE COMPANY OWNERSHIP\par \par \uc2 Zimbabwe and Zimplats , the local unit of\par \par \uc2 the world's second-largest platinum producer\par \par \uc2 Impala Platinum\uc2  , said on Tuesday they had\par \par \uc2 agreed to produce a revised plan for a law\par \par \uc2 requiring mining firms to turn over a 51 percent\par \par \uc2 stake to local blacks.\par \par \uc2 BOTSWANA CERTIFICATES YIELDS\par \par \uc2 The weighted average yield on Botswana 14-day\par \par \uc2 certificates slipped to 6.56 percent from 6.57\par \par \uc2 percent a week ago, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on\par \par \uc2 Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 RWANDA POWER\par \par \uc2 Egypt's \uc2 Orascom Construction Industries\par \par \uc2 plans to invest up to $130 million in Rwanda in\par \par \uc2 the next three to four years to build a methane\par \par \uc2 power plant to produce 50 megawatts, a company\par \par \uc2 official said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 SOMALIA SECURITY\par \par \uc2 World powers should take advantage of a retreat by\par \par \uc2 Somalia's al Shabaab rebels and step up efforts to\par \par \uc2 defeat them by backing government troops and\par \par \uc2 imposing a no-fly zone and a sea blockade, the\par \par \uc2 African Union said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 * Somali security forces briefly detained two\par \par \uc2 Turkish aid workers on Tuesday after they\par \par \uc2 delivered food to famine victims in an area near\par \par \uc2 the capital controlled by rebels, officials said\par \par \uc2 on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 For the latest precious metals report click on\par \par \uc2 For the latest base metals report click on\par \par \uc2 For the latest crude oil report click on\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 94.450 Kenyan Shillings) ($1 = 28.525 Mauritius Rupees)\par \par \uc2 AFRICA-FACTORS/   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110917e79e0003q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pic