\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Kenya \highlight\uc2  shilling eases, cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  eyed\b0\par\par\uc2 495 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 2011\par 07:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Interbank lending, discount window rates fall\par \par \uc2 * Market watching \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  for further dollar selling\par \par \uc2 * Shilling weakens as importers buy dollars\par \par \uc2 (Adds discount window rate, shilling)\par \par \uc2 By Kevin Mwanza\par \par \uc2 NAIROBI, Sept 7 (Reuters) - Kenya's shilling eased slightly on Wednesday as importers rushed to buy dollars after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  started selling the greenback to stem a rout in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has already fallen about 15 percent this year.\par \par \uc2 The shilling had gained as much as 2.4 percent against the dollar on Tuesday after traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sold dollars for the first time in two years. The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  itself declined to comment on any such move.\par \par \uc2 The more aggressive stance against a prolonged weakening of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  took the markets by surprise. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Njuguna Ndung'u has said in the past that selling dollars would not achieve much and would drive \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves down.\par \par \uc2 At 0850 GMT, commercial banks quoted the shilling at 93.70/90 against the dollar, slightly weaker than Tuesday's close of 93.50/60.\par \par \uc2 Traders said importers were taking advantage of the earlier gain to stock up on dollars, which could weaken the shilling somewhat, and they expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell more dollars during the session to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "At lower (stronger shilling) levels there will be some customer dollar demand. Right now, the market will keep a look out on what the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does. That's an important factor," said a trader at one commercial bank.\par \par \uc2 Kenya's weighted average interbank lending rate and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's discount window rate fell further on Wednesday, continuing a trend seen since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  changed its policy for calculating the discount window rate.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has tamed sky-high money market rates with the policy adjustment, but analysts say it still faces a struggle to restore market confidence.\par \par \uc2 The weighted average interbank lending rate fell to 10.4006 percent from 12.1424 percent on Tuesday, while the discount window rate fell to 11.76 percent from 12.68 percent previously.\par \par \uc2 The bank is now using a moving average of interbank rates over an unspecified period to compute its discount window rate, in a move it hopes will boost shilling liquidity after a sharp funding squeeze.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday it would hold an unscheduled Monetary Policy Committee meeting on Sep. 14, which analysts said might be used to push up the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Rate, giving the shilling some support. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ...........................Shilling spot rates \par <0#KESF=>.....................Shilling forward rates \par .......................Cross rates \par ..................................Local contributors \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 .......................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Kenya\f28 \uc2 \f2  Index \par .....................Kenyan Bonds contributor pages \par ...............Treasury bill yields \par ..................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par .........................Horizontal repo transactions \par , ................Daily interbank lending rate \par <0#KETSYSTR=>.............................Kenya Bond pricing \par ..................Real time Africa economic data \par <ECI & AFR> ...........................African economic news \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SPEED GUIDES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Editing by Yara Bayoumy)\f28 \par \par \uc2 KENYA-MARKETS/ (UPDATE 1) (REFILE)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110910e79700033\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
