\par\par \b \uc2 AFRICA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  WEEKAHEAD-Kenya, Uganda shillings stay under pressure\b0\par\par\uc2 1,398 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 2011\par 16:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 NAIROBI, July 7 (Reuters) - Kenya's and Uganda's shillings are likely to come under pressure against the dollar next week, while Tanzania's steadily weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  may take brief respite after unusually stiff \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 KENYA\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2 's shilling <KES=> is seen weaker against the dollar next week, pressured by expected dollar demand from the energy sector and maize importers, traders said.\par \par \uc2 Kenya is predicting increased maize importation after the government removed duties in June to address shortages and rising prices of the staple. [ID:nLDE75K0FF]\par \par \uc2 At 0822 GMT, the shilling was posted at 89.75/89.85 against the dollar, weaker than last Thursday's close of 89.35/55.\par \par \uc2 "At the moment energy sector and also maize sector dollar demand might come in, pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weaker. We might see a weaker shilling in the coming week," said Bhavin Chandaria, a trader at \uc2 Imperial Bank\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Njuguna Ndung'u said on Thursday that poor reading of information by market participants was to blame for fresh shilling weakness against the dollar. [ID:nLDE7660P8]\par \par \uc2 Traders said they expected the shilling to trade in the 89.80-91.00 range.\par \par \uc2 The shilling has gained since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its overnight lending rate to 8.0 percent, lifting it off a record low of 91.90 against the dollar on June 22. [ID:nLDE75S0QW]\par \par \uc2 "The shilling seems to be in dire straits again and is likely to be dragged lower if other dollar buyers join the fray," \uc2 Commercial Bank of Africa\uc2  said in a note.\par \par \uc2 UGANDA\par \par \uc2 The Uganda shilling will stay under pressure against the dollar next week, despite the introduction of a new benchmark lending rate, traders in the capital, Kampala, said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bank of Uganda\uc2  launched the inaugural benchmark interest rate of 13 percent and a 5 percent core inflation target on Wednesday in a bid to tame price pressures that pushed inflation to a 17-year high in May.\par \par \uc2 But with dollar inflows expected to remain tight and demand from the oil sector high, traders do not see it having an immediate impact on what the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says is an undervalued \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The shilling sold for 2,600/2,620 to the dollar towards the end of trade on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "Unless the fundamentals change I see it holding at these levels," Lucas Ochieng, treasurer at Orient Bank Uganda, said. "Liquidity is still the issue, so even given the introduction of the CBR, we will still see the status quo."\par \par \uc2 Some analysts had said it might take the Ugandan shilling time to respond, but that the tight monetary policy stance meant the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  should continue its climb from June's all-time lows against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "There will be more pressure next week," Faisal Bukenya, head of market making at Barclays Uganda, said. "We're not seeing the inflows."\par \par \uc2 Traders, though, did expect a pick-up in interest for short-term paper from offshore investors.\par \par \uc2 The shilling slipped to a record low of 2,710 against the dollar last week on strong dollar demand from the oil sector, speculative trading and panic buying before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in and sold dollars.\par \par \uc2 TANZANIA\par \par \uc2 Tanzania's shilling <TZS=> is expected to hold steady after firming slightly against the dollar on Wednesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved to calm the market.\par \par \uc2 Commercial banks quoted it at 1,600/1,605 to the dollar at Wednesday's close, after earlier trading at an all-time low of 1,625.\par \par \uc2 Markets are closed in Tanzania on Thursday for a public holiday.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor met bankers this week and told them that he would like to see the shilling trading below 1,600 in the interbank market," United Bank of Africa Tanzania dealer Bernard Charo said, referring to one of the regular meetings held with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded $17.85 million on its interbank market, more than double its daily average amount for the year, traders said.\par \par \uc2 But traders said they did not expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sustain higher dollar sales after the government said it did not want to deplete \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. [ID:nLDE75K207]\par \par \uc2 "Some corporate customers are standing aside, waiting for the shilling to continue to depreciate before they come in with their demand for dollars," said Johnvian Nyamsisa, a trader at Commercial Bank of Africa Tanzania.\par \par \uc2 "The shilling might go to 1,590-1,600 levels next week if the current demand slowdown continues."\par \par \uc2 In the week to Wednesday, the \uc2 Bank of Tanzania\uc2  traded $45.55 million on the Interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Market, according to its website.\par \par \uc2 ZAMBIA\par \par \uc2 The kwacha <ZMK=> is expected to firm as foreign investors convert dollars in order to pay local taxes.\par \par \uc2 Commercial banks quoted the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Africa's leading copper producer at 4,820, marginally up from 4,830 to the dollar a week ago.\par \par \uc2 "The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to post some gains against the dollar with the anticipated increase in dollar supply from corporates who will be converting foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for kwacha in order meet statutory obligations," Cavmont bank treasurer Mudenda Syamujaye said.\par \par \uc2 The kwacha has traded between 4,800 and 4,600 for most of this year. During 2010 it met firm resistance at 4,600. On the few occasions it breached that level it went on to test, but failed to breach, 4,550.\par \par \uc2 GHANA\par \par \uc2 The cedi <GHS=> is seen holding firm against the dollar ahead of the issue of a 5-year bond open to foreigners on July 28, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The unit is likely to close the week at 1.5160 versus the greenback and will remain steady at that level, said Jacob Brobbey of \uc2 Barclays Ghana\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We see rates tamed in the $1.5120-$1.5160 band in the coming weeks," he said.\par \par \uc2 Ghana's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has announced plans to issue a 300 million cedi bond on July 28, the first 5-year note since December 2007.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the bank's Monetary Policy Committee announced a 50 basis point cut on its benchmark rate to 12.5 percent, which analysts said boosted the resilience of the cedi.\par \par \uc2 Biggles Amponsah of Access Bank Ghana projected a balanced dollar flows.\par \par \uc2 "I will also expect traders to start shorting the dollar in smaller volumes ahead of the bond issue. This should be sufficient reason to hold the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar amidst rising demand," he said.\par \par \uc2 NIGERIA\par \par \uc2 The naira <NGN=D1> is seen losing ground as traders miss out on dollars expected to be sold by state-oil firm NNPC, which instead went to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The state-owned energy company usually sells dollars to some lenders on a monthly basis and transfers the naira proceeds to its account with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . NNPC dollar sales usually form the bulk of supplies to the interbank market.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading at 153.32 to the dollar on the interbank on Thursday compared with 152.60 at Wednesday's close as traders contended with lower-than-expected month-end dollar inflows.\par \par \uc2 "With the NNPC funds no longer available for trading at the interbank market, the naira will definitely depreciate further in the coming days," one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader said.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said the naira should trade within a 153-153.90 band.\par \par \uc2 "We are hoping that some foreign investors bring in dollars next week to help provide some liquidity in the market in view of the present reality and cushion the impact of the absence of NNPC dollars in the market," another dealer said.\par \par \uc2 The naira appreciated to its strongest level in six months last week after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  initiated measures aimed at boosting dollar supply, reducing pressure on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  this month lifted a rule that foreign investors hold government debt for at least one year, a move which is expected to attract new offshore flows, boosting dollar supply and increasing demand for the naira.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also imposed a maximum weekly limit of $250,000 in dollar sales by banks to \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  bureaux, a move which traders said was to check money laundering and capital flight, contributing to naira support.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Kevin Mwanza, Fumbuka Ng'wanakilala, Barry Malone, Chris Mfula, Oludare Mayowa and Kwasi Kpodo, editing by Ed Cropley)\par \par \uc2 AFRICA-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 /   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110707e777000zk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
