\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Kenyan c.bank says has acted on  \highlight22\uc2 fx \highlight\uc2  speculation\b0\par\par\uc2 653 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juni 2011\par 15:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Says has taken action to stop arbitrage\par \par \uc2 * Says further tightening being considered\par \par \uc2 (Adds more quotes, analyst)\par \par \uc2 By Duncan Miriri\par \par \uc2 NAIROBI, June 23 (Reuters) - Kenya's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has taken unspecified action against some commercial banks to curb speculative positions versus the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of east Africa's largest economy, its governor said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The shilling hit a new low against the dollar of 91.90 on Wednesday but recovered on Thursday to end at 90.1 after a report the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would take steps to stem the trades.\par \par \uc2 "We have taken action on them and we cannot talk about what action we have taken because it's regulatory. We have taken proper action on them, appropriate to the law, and we'll continuously do that," Governor Njuguna Ndung'u told a news conference. "We are not afraid to do that again."\par \par \uc2 The market had closed before he made these comments.\par \par \uc2 Inflation in Kenya has surged into double-digits this year reaching 12.95 percent in May. Short-dated Treasury bond yields have jumped into double-digits and the shilling has lost more than 10 percent since 2010.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures follow an audit of banks' trading positions. Ndung'u said that during the week of June 9, five banks exported $260 million while borrowing from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's window by strong banks went up -- pointing to arbitrage.\par \par \uc2 "These positions do not seem to reflect trading fundamentals. This type of exposure will put pressure on the exchange rate ... We will restrict them from any arbitrage using the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. "We cannot ratify arbitrage."\par \par \uc2 Under the law establishing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the regulator can direct the management of a commercial bank to provide a viable explanation for any adverse effects in the market, and even speculative behaviour, the governor has said.\par \par \uc2 He has said that if such speculative behaviour were not halted, section 32 A of the Banking Act gave the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  the power to act. The section allows the regulator to apply sanctions up to disqualification against people managing or controlling financial institutions.\par \par \uc2 TIGHTER POLICY?\par \par \uc2 "The arbitrage opportunity -- that has allowed banks with healthy liquidity positions to borrow cheaply at the overnight window of the CBK, and reinvest proceeds in higher yielding short-term T-bills, or fund other trades -- has been identified," said Razia Khan, head of Africa research at Standard Chartered Bank in London.\par \par \uc2 "Although it is unclear just yet how the authorities will deal with this, some tightening of liquidity should be anticipated," she said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has resisted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by selling hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the shilling's slide. Ndung'u said \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2  had adequate \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves but could only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stabilise \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility, rather than the level or direction of the shilling.\par \par \uc2 He said the bank might in future consider further tightening of monetary policy if inflation was not tame.\par \par \uc2 "But we are seeing signs ... that even though inflation will not come down drastically, the signs are inflation will come down and we are waiting on inflationary expectations."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its benchmark lending rate by 25 basis points in January but reversed the move in March and raised rates by another 25 basis points in May to 6.25 percent.\par \par \uc2 "With the regulator now taking firmer action against continued shilling depreciation -- albeit still within the confines of allowing markets to determine the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate -- a lower peak in inflation appears more likely," said Khan.\par \par \uc2 "Actual shilling appreciation would, however, be needed to meaningfully improve the near term inflation outlook," she said.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Kevin Mwanza and Richard Lough; editing by David Clarke and Stephen Nisbet\par \par \uc2 (For more Reuters Africa coverage and to have your say on the top issues, visit: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://af.reuters.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://af.reuters.com/}}}\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 KENYA-GOVERNOR/ (UPDATE 2)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110626e76n000bh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
