\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Kenya shilling plunges to new record low vs dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 700 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juni 2011\par 10:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Shilling hits 91 after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Oil sector dollar demand seen weighing on the shilling\par \par \uc2 * Stocks flat on weak economic outlook\par \par \uc2 (Recast with markets close, stocks, bonds)\par \par \uc2 By Kevin Mwanza\par \par \uc2 NAIROBI, June 20 (Reuters) - The Kenyan shilling <KES=> tumbled to a record low of 91.00 against the dollar on Monday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the shilling, traders said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2  (CBK) Governor Njuguna Ndung'u said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market at this stage to prop up the shilling would make things worse for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as some of its problems stem from concerns about the euro zone. [ID:nLDE75J0O6]\par \par \uc2 At close of trade at 1300 GMT, the shilling was quoted at the session low of 91.0, a 1.4 percent depreciation from Friday's close of 89.7.\par \par \uc2 "I think the move started on the back of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments that made the market panic some more," said a senior trader at one commercial bank who did not want to be named.\par \par \uc2 Ndung'u was reacting to analyst comments that the bank needed to do more than just increase interest rates to counter a vicious inflation shock that has driven an 11.6 percent slide in the shilling this year. [ID:nLDE7580LQ]\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had also planned to mop up 0.5 billion shillings ($5.6 million) through repurchase agreements, but rejected all the bids for the third straight session. <CBK04>\par \par \uc2 The bank's repurchase agreements, or repos, basically take shillings out of the market to tighten liquidity.\par \par \uc2 Traders said earlier that interbank trading limits were tight following aggressive trading last week that saw the shilling touch a string of all-time lows.\par \par \uc2 They said the shilling could face further pressure this week as end-month corporate demand for dollars, especially form the oil sector, came in to the market.\par \par \uc2 "There is no liquidity in the market. It dried on the governor's comments. In a sane environment, the resistance would be 92. But now the sky is the limit," said Chris Muiga, senior trader at Kenya Commercial Bank.\par \par \uc2 "Corporate end-month demand from the oil sector may keep the shilling under pressure this week," said Steve Lagat, a trader at \uc2 CFC Stanbic Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On the Nairobi Stock Exchange, the benchmark NSE-20 Share Index <.NSE20> was barely changed, edging slightly up by 0.03 percent to 3,986.05 points.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said the weaker economic outlook due to the rising inflation rate and the volatile shilling was affecting market activities on the bourse.\par \par \uc2 "The market is very bearish and its being affected by the performance of the shilling and a high inflation rate," said Renaldo D'souza of Genghis Capital.\par \par \uc2 "Rising interest rates in the fixed income market has also curbed new investment from the equities market."\par \par \uc2 Yields on Treasury bills have been on the rise for the last few weeks, but started easing lasting week after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the cost of government debt had become too expensive. [ID:nLDE75F1MB]\par \par \uc2 Shares in Williamson Tea rose 3.81 percent to 218 shillings after it announced a 9 percent rise in full-year pretax profits, boosted by an increase in property valuations. [ID:nLDE75J05R]\par \par \uc2 Barclays Bank of Kenya shares rose 2.07 percent to 17.25 shillings a share on foreign investors buys, traders said.\par \par \uc2 Corporate and Treasury bonds valued at 2.82 billion shillings ($31.4 million) were traded on the stock exchange, down from 4.805 billion shillings on Friday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par       \par  <KES=> <KES1=>...........................Shilling spot rates\par  <KESF=> <0#KESF=>.....................Shilling forward rates\par  <EURKES=> <KESX=> <KESX1=>.......................Cross rates\par  <KES=KE>..................................Local contributors\par  <CBKINDEX>\f28 \uc2 \f2 .......................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Kenya\f28 \uc2 \f2  Index\par  <KE/DEBT>.....................Kenyan Bonds contributor pages\par  <CBK03> <CBK06> <KE3MTB=>...............Treasury bill yields\par  <CBK04>..................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par  <CBK07>.........................Horizontal repo transactions\par  <KEIBR=>,<CBK02>................Daily interbank lending rate\par  <0#KETSYSTR=>.............................Kenya Bond pricing\par  <ECONAFRICA>..................Real time Africa economic data\par  <ECI & AFR> ...........................African economic news\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SPEED GUIDES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 <REUTERS> <KES/1> <KE/DEBT> <MONEY> <KE/EQUITY>\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by George Obulutsa and Beatrice Gachenge; Editing by David Clarke)\f28 \par \par \uc2 KENYA-MARKETS/ (UPDATE 3)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110623e76k000f1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
