\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-AFRICA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  WEEKAHEAD-Kenya shilling to test record low\b0\par\par\uc2 1,100 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 07:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (repeats with no change to text)\par \par \uc2 NAIROBI, March 3 (Reuters) - The Kenyan, Ugandan and Tanzanian shillings are all likely to fall towards record lows next week amid strong demand for dollars from oil importers. Strong \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not expected.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 KENYA\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2 's shilling <KES=> is seen easing towards a lifetime low due to hefty demand for dollars from oil importers, companies paying dividends abroad and the government signalling it will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Commercial banks quoted the shilling at 83.00/10 to the dollar -- 6-1/2 year lows -- compared with last Thursday's close of 82.00/10. Its lifetime low is 83.35, touched on Aug 25, 2004.\par \par \uc2 "There's a congruence of several factors working against the shilling. We have seen oil guys are really active. On top of that interest rates are really low and it's dividend season so the multinationals are repatriating," said Chris Muiga, senior trader at Kenya Commercial Bank.\par \par \uc2 "Then the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  comes out and says 'We're cool with the weak shilling'. When you put all this together it just points to one direction. I think the market will continue to test higher levels."\par \par \uc2 Treasury Permanent Secretary Joseph Kinyua said on Wednesday the shilling's decline was not worrying, adding that it would be good for the export sector. [nLDE7210OY]\par \par \uc2 A spike in world oil prices due to turmoil in the Middle East has also made Kenyan importers nervous.\par \par \uc2 "Oil importers have geared up for new oil consignments as they fear prices will go higher in light of the crisis in Libya," said Edwin Mathenge, a senior trader at Chase Bank.\par \par \uc2 Traders said they expect the shilling to trade in the 82.50-83.50 range. Charts suggest the shilling is in a long-term downtrend and has further to fall. [ID:nLDE71R0ZE]\par \par \uc2 TANZANIA\par \par \uc2 Tanzania's shilling <TZS=> is also expected to weaken towards a record low as companies pay dividends to offshore shareholders.\par \par \uc2 Commercial banks quoted the shilling at 1,513/1,518 to the dollar compared with 1,512/1,514 at last Thursday's close. The unit is off this week's four-month low of 1,518, a level last seen in September.\par \par \uc2 It hit a record low of 1,527 in May last year, but traders said corporate dollar demand could push it to as low as 1,540 by June.\par \par \uc2 "Many companies, especially those with shareholders outside the country, are expected to pay dividends to parent companies and thus repatriation of dollars will push the shilling further down," said National Bank of Commerce economist Yono Mtengule.\par \par \uc2 Dollar inflows from agriculture, one of the main sources of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , are unlikely to start any time soon.\par \par \uc2 "Inflows are quite limited. We expect agricultural exports such as cashew to start in April. That's when we'll see significant inflows," said Rahim Suleiman, a trader at African Banking Corporation Tanzania.\par \par \uc2 Between last Thursday and Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded $31.15 million on its Interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Market, statistics on its website showed.\par \par \uc2 In July to December, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the main source of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , selling $551 million out of a total $881 million traded, according to its February monetary policy statement. [ID:nLDE7210JV]\par \par \uc2 UGANDA\par \par \uc2 Having rebounded strongly after peaceful presidential elections last month, Uganda's shilling <UGX=> is likely to fall due to weak dollar inflows and an absence of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Commercial banks quoted the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 2,369/2,374 from last Thursday's close of 2,345/2,350. Some traders see the unit testing the key psychological level of 2,400 -- an all-time low plumbed in mid-January.\par \par \uc2 "If you look at the usual month-end demand together with an aspect of covering for dividends, I see the shilling weakening," said Lucas Ochieng, a trader at Orient Bank Uganda. "The inflows are not meeting demand."\par \par \uc2 Traders see the shilling trading in the 2,375-2,395 range into next week.\par \par \uc2 "Inflows are not healthy," said Faisal Bukenya, head of market making at Barclays Bank Uganda. "Even those who are even converting dollars are converting small amounts."\par \par \uc2 After January's record low, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  pledged to beef up dollar supply, although traders said it was unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week.\par \par \uc2 The shilling neared a nine-day low, when it touched 2,370 on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 ZAMBIA\par \par \uc2 The kwacha <ZMK=> is likely to firm as general dollar weakness across the G10 \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  trickles down to emerging markets. Commercial banks quoted it at 4,715 versus 4,740 a week ago.\par \par \uc2 Standard Chartered's local head of global markets Stanley Tamele said exporters had injected sizeable amounts of dollars into the market but this was being met with aggressive bids mainly from offshore banks and importers.\par \par \uc2 "The spike in oil prices above $110 per barrel has also reignited dollar demand from some oil marketing companies. The market is likely to consolidate between 4700-4800," Tamele said.\par \par \uc2 The kwacha met firm resistance around 4,600 during 2010. On the few occasions it breached that level, and went on to test but failed to breach 4,550.\par \par \uc2 GHANA\par \par \uc2 The cedi <GHS=> is likely to come under pressure due to dollar demand from manufacturers ahead of Easter and the impact of high crude oil prices.\par \par \uc2 The cedi was at 1.52 to the dollar on Thursday, weaker than 1.4950 touched on Feb. 17, and moving towards a lifetime low of 1.5790 hit a month ago.\par \par \uc2 Dollar inflows ahead of a 3-year bond auction open to foreigners accounted for much of the cedi's appreciation from those depths. Without that support, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to weaken to 1.53, said Biggles Amponsah of Access Bank.\par \par \uc2 "These gains could not be sustained as they were highly backed by the USD inflow from the offshore investors, and not a significant improvement in economic activities," he said.\par \par \uc2 However, Databank's Sampson Akligoh said the cedi would hold its ground if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stuck to its policy of regularly selling dollars.\par \par \uc2 "I am concerned about the impact of higher crude oil prices on Ghana's trade balance. This would induce depreciation pressures, which can only be contained by Bank of Ghana's participation in the market," Agligoh said. (Reporting by Kevin Mwanza, George Obulutsa, Fumbuka Ng'wanakilala, Barry Malone, Chris Mfula, Hereward Holland and Oludare Mayowa; Editing by Ron Askew)\par \par \uc2 AFRICA-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 /|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|AFN|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110304e734000d2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley