\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Weakening Kenyan shilling not detrimental -finmin\b0\par\par\uc2 342 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 10:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Authorities will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  just yet\par \par \uc2 * Not worried because weakening is manageable\par \par \uc2 * Easing shilling good for exporters\par \par \uc2 (Adds details, quotes)\par \par \uc2 NAIROBI, March 2 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in favour of the shilling <KES=> against the dollar just yet because its weakening is manageable and not destructive to business, a top Finance Ministry official said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The Kenyan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is sliding towards an all-time low and touched 83.10/20 earlier on Wednesday -- its lowest level since hitting a record low of 83.35 on Aug. 25, 2004.\par \par \uc2 "We shall not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  just yet. We do not think the current weakening is destructive to business in terms of decision making," Joseph Kinyua, permanent secretary at the Finance Ministry, told reporters.\par \par \uc2 "I don't think we would be so much worried with manageable weakening because we still need the shilling to reflect the reality of the market, and it is good for the export business because if we take policies that are too hard, it will hurt them," he said.\par \par \uc2 Technical analysis shows the shilling has further to fall in coming weeks. [ID:nLDE71R0ZE]\par \par \uc2 Kinyua said the government wanted a competitive shilling that would support exporters too.\par \par \uc2 "If it becomes too strong it may be okay from a national pride (perspective) but not in terms of promoting prosperity and economic growth," he said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases last week, the first time it has done so this year after a series of purchases last year.\par \par \uc2 It maintains that its participation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is purely to beef up its reserves, and not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Of course the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be keeping watch of what is happening in terms of interest rates and exchange rates to ensure that they are not moving in a manner which can be destructive to economic activity," Kinyua said. (Reporting by Beatrice Gachenge; Editing by Helen Nyambura-Mwaura and Catherine Evans)\par \par \uc2 KENYA-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|AFN|ABN|M|D|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110305e73200045\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
