\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Kenyan shilling firms vs dollar, stocks ease\b0\par\par\uc2 650 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 September 2010\par 12:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  investors square off ahead of weekend\par \par \uc2 * Bond trading quiet\par \par \uc2 * MPC decision positive but already priced in\par \par \uc2 * Main NSE-20 share index closes lower\par \par \uc2 (Adds market close, details)\par \par \uc2 By Richard Lough and George Obulutsa\par \par \uc2 NAIROBI, Sept 24 (Reuters) - Kenya's shilling firmed slightly against the dollar on Friday as investors squared off positions ahead of the weekend while the main index on the Nairobi Stock Exchange (NSE) eased.\par \par \uc2 At the close of trade at 1300 GMT, commercial banks quoted the shilling <KES=> at 80.90/81.00 to the dollar, compared with Thursday's close of 81.15/25, and slightly stronger than 80.95/81.05 where the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded earlier in the day.\par \par \uc2 "We're seeing squaring off of positions ahead of the weekend. Also, whenever it gets above 81.00 importer demand for dollars subsides," said Moses Kiboi, head of trading at Citi.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the widely expected decision by Kenya's Monetary Policy Committee (MPC) to leave the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's benchmark lending rate steady at 6 percent sent out positive signals over the economy's health but had already been factored into prices. [ID:nLDE68M1HV]\par \par \uc2 Technical analysis showed the dollar resistance level of 80.80 with the 50-day moving average standing at 80.59.\par \par \uc2 Traders will also keep an eye on the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Kenya\uc2 , which has bought dollars in the market recently, frustrating some market players who say the shilling's fundamentals are stronger than its price.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still buying dollars. Anything below 81.00 is fantastic for them and we could see them picking up quite a bit," said Peter Mutuku, head of corporate desk at Bank of Africa \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday that it does not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless the market was unstable and highly volatile.\par \par \uc2 It also said that in making foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases, it did so to meet its minimum threshold and pay for the government's external obligations. [ID:nLDE68M1RY]\par \par \uc2 Kiboi said bond trading was sluggish with most demand targeting a 2-year Treasury bond at rates between 3.75 - 4.0 percent.\par \par \uc2 Kenya accepted bids worth 13.4 billion shillings for the two-year bond at auction on Wednesday after receiving a 3 percent oversubscription. The weighted average rate was 3.698 percent. [ID:nWEA925]\par \par \uc2 On the NSE, shares in Kenyan fuel marketer KenolKobil rose to their highest since July after the firm said it expects its crude oil import licence to be re-instated following the end of a protracted dispute with the country's sole refinery. [ID:nLDE68N0C0]\par \par \uc2 The shares rose 7 percent to end at 10.10 shillings after rising 9.5 percent to 10.35 shillings in earlier on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Kenya Power and Lighting Company closed 3 percent lower at 238 shillings after its full year results failed to meet market expectations, traders said.\par \par \uc2 In earlier trade, the shares fell 10 percent to a low of 220 shillings compared with Thursday's close.\par \par \uc2 Corporate and government bonds worth 475.2 million shillings were traded at the bourse, compared with 275.9 million shillings traded on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The main NSE-20 share index <.NSE20> closed 20.09 points lower at 4,581.72.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par <KES=> <KES1=>...........................Shilling spot rates \par <KESF=> <0#KESF=>.....................Shilling forward rates \par <EURKES=> <KESX=> <KESX1=>.......................Cross rates \par <KES=KE>..................................Local contributors \par <CBKINDEX>\f28 \uc2 \f2 .......................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Kenya\f28 \uc2 \f2  Index \par <KE/DEBT>.....................Kenyan Bonds contributor pages \par <CBK03> <CBK06> <KE3MTB=>...............Treasury bill yields \par <CBK04>..................\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par <CBK07>.........................Horizontal repo transactions \par <KEIBR=>,<CBK02>................Daily interbank lending rate \par <0#KETSYSTR=>.............................Kenya Bond pricing \par <ECONAFRICA>..................Real time Africa economic data \par <ECI & AFR> ...........................African economic news \par SPEED GUIDES:     <REUTERS> <KES/1> <KE/DEBT> <MONEY> \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 <KE/EQUITY> (Editing by James Macharia and Toby Chopra)\f28 \par \par \uc2 KENYA-MARKETS/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|AFN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100927e69o000ph\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
