\par\par \b \uc2 Kenya unit slides marginally as cbank buys dlrs\b0\par\par\uc2 339 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 April 2009\par 13:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 NAIROBI, April 30 (Reuters) - Kenya's shilling <KES=> softened marginally versus the dollar on Thursday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered to buy $10 million and traders did not expect it to strengthen past the 78.50 level in coming days.\par \par \uc2 At 1100 GMT, commercial banks posted the unit at 78.65/75 per dollar compared with 78.55/65 at Wednesday's close.\par \par \uc2 "We've seen the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  two days in a row now for monetary policy purposes," said Steve Lagat, a trader at CFC Stanbic Bank. "People are still watching to see if they keep buying."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which rarely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, has purchased a total $30 million since last Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "Liquidity has been tight in the money market so they are killing two birds with one stone. They have to raise reserves as well," Lagat said.\par \par \uc2 Official \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have fallen far below the statutory requirement of four months import cover.\par \par \uc2 Dealers expect the shilling to face resistance at the 78.50 level.\par \par \uc2 "The shillings's ascent could be checked by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's activities in the market," a report by Bank of Africa said. "The market will also keep an eye on the happenings on the political front where any negative sentiments might send the shilling tumbling."\par \par \uc2 Kenya's coalition government partners have been bickering over who should run an influential parlimentary committee, heightening tensions and fears of a return to days of turmoil.\par \par \uc2 Kenyan markets are closed on Friday to mark Labour Day. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  <KES=> <KES1=>................Shilling spot rates\par  <KESF=>....................Shilling forward rates\par  <EURKES=> <KESX=>.....................Cross rates\par  <KE/CONT1>.................All Kenya Contributors\par  <CBKINDEX>............\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Kenya Index\par  <KE/DEBT>..........Kenyan Bonds contributor pages       \par  <CBK03> <CBK06> <KE3MTB=>....Treasury bill yields\par  <KEIBR=> <CBK02>.....Daily interbank lending rate\par  <0#KETSY=>.....................Kenya Bond pricing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SPEED GUIDES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 <REUTERS> <KES/1> <KE/DEBT> <MONEY> (Reporting by Helen Nyambura-Mwaura)\f28 \par \par \uc2 KENYA-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 /|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|AFN|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090503e54u00074\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
