\par\par \b \uc2 Kenya shilling tumbles vs dlr, market eyes c.bank\b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Oktober 2008\par 10:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 NAIROBI, Oct 22 (Reuters) - Kenya's shilling <KES=> tumbled against the dollar on Wednesday on interbank greenback purchases, touching a near four-year low as the market focused on the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2  for any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At 0750 GMT, leading commercial banks posted the unit at 79.20/30 against the broadly strong dollar, compared with Tuesday's close of 78.10/20.\par \par \uc2 The 79.00 level was last seen in December 2004 and traders said the unit could close the session weaker than 79.00, barring \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The unit has weakened 8.5 percent in October as the effects of the global credit crunch spread to the east African nation.\par \par \uc2 "These are the levels around which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  came in last week and although the shilling still remains under pressure, guys are hesitant," a dealer with a commercial bank said.\par \par \uc2 Traders said there was light dollar demand by importers in the hope of another \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 -backed rally.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in last Friday, selling an unspecified amount of dollars, according to some dealers, causing the local unit to rally.\par \par \uc2 "Importers are hoping that they will see some retracement and holding off where they can and only buying what they need to buy now," said the dealer.\par \par \uc2 Jackie Maina, an Equity Bank dealer, said fundamentals were working against the shilling due to factors such as the global crisis which analysts expect to affect the country's tourism.\par \par \uc2 The sector earned the country $1 billion last year and is just beginning to recover from the effects of a bloody post-election crisis in January and February.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  <KES=> <KES1=>............Shilling spot rates\par  <KESF=>...............Shilling forward rates       \par  <EURKES=>    <KESX=>.Cross rates\par  <KE/CONT1=>............All Kenya Contributors\par  <CBKINDEX>\f28 \uc2 \f2 ........\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Kenya\f28 \uc2 \f2  Index\par  <KE/DEBT>......Kenyan Bonds contributor pages       \par  <CBK03>    <CBK06> <KE3MTB=>.    Treasury bill yields\par  <KEIBR=>,<CBK02>    Daily interbank lending rate\par  <0#KETSY=>    Kenya Bond pricing         \par  SPEED GUIDES:                              \par  <REUTERS> <KES/1> <KE/DEBT> <MONEY>  #\par  (Reporting by Duncan Miriri; Editing by David Stamp)   \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 KENYA-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 /|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|AFN|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081022e4am000m1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
